  beats = {["defias.hideout"]={d={155,92747},b={"Edwin VanCleef"}},["defias.juggernaut"]={d={166},b={"Edwin VanCleef"}},["defias.masons"]={d={135,141,373},b={"Edwin VanCleef"}},["prestor.onyxia"]={},["q1016.2"]={d={1016}},["q1022.6"]={d={1043}},["q1195.3"]={d={1196}},["q120.5"]={d={146}},["q123.3"]={d={147}},["q1274.5"]={d={1249}},["q1480.4"]={d={1482}},["q1483.3"]={d={1094}},["q164.5"]={d={268}},["q165.5"]={d={252}},["q2098.3"]={d={2078}},["q288.4"]={d={290}},["q303.3"]={d={303}},["q358.4"]={d={357}},["q373.5"]={d={393}},["q421.5"]={d={424}},["q437.6"]={d={444}},["q4542.4"]={d={5064}},["q463.2"]={d={463}},["q477.3"]={d={481}},["q4821.5"]={d={5088}},["q488.2"]={d={488}},["q5.2"]={d={5}},["q533.4"]={d={506}},["q533.6"]={d={508}},["q5726.2"]={d={5726}},["q5726.3"]={d={5727}},["q6421.2"]={d={6421}},["q65.7"]={d={166}},["q66.6"]={d={80}},["q66.7"]={d={97}},["q867.3"]={d={875}},["q886.5"]={d={1489}},["q886.6"]={d={1490}},["q94.4"]={d={248}},["q954.5"]={d={957}},["q96392.4"]={d={96391}},["q965.3"]={d={970}},["unsent.lescovar"]={d={434}}},
  recaps = {[219]={k="373",mid={d=350,t="You struck down Edwin VanCleef and discovered a letter addressed to Baros Alexston in Stormwind. Baros revealed their past in the Stonemasons Guild, cheated by the nobility, which drove VanCleef to rebellion. Seeking answers, you ventured into the rioting Stockade and executed VanCleef's lieutenant, Bazil Thredd. This grim act earned Warden Thelwater's trust. He spoke of a mysterious visitor who frequently met with Thredd. Master Mathias Shaw of SI:7 identified this visitor as an assassin named Marzon, serving the corrupt Lord Gregor Lescovar. Exposing a noble's ties to the Defias Brotherhood requires undeniable proof now that VanCleef and Thredd lie dead. You have sought the reluctant aid of Elling Trias to unravel the conspiracy. What true depths this corruption reaches, and how you can pierce a noble's untouchable standing, remains unknown."},["end"]={d=396,t="You found an unsent letter on Edwin VanCleef, exposing his bitter vendetta against Stormwind's nobility. Following a trail from the riotous Stockade to the shadows of Old Town, you uncovered a conspiracy reaching the city's highest ranks. With covert aid from SI:7 and a daring gnome, you eliminated the corrupt Lord Gregor Lescovar and his assassin in the castle gardens. The Defias Brotherhood's plot to ruin the kingdom was dismantled in silence. Though the king was away, Lady Katrana Prestor received your report in Stormwind Keep. Your unspoken justice saved the city from a terrible revenge, leaving its nobles wholly oblivious to their narrow escape."},before={a=391,t="From the corpse of Edwin VanCleef, you pulled an unsent letter meant for Baros Alexston, Stormwind's City Architect. When you delivered the parchment, the architect recognized the hand of a man consumed by vengeance. He spoke of the Stonemasons Guild, of how they rebuilt the city after the war only for the ruling nobles to cheat them of their pay. VanCleef sparked a riot before vanishing into the wild. To unravel what schemes the mastermind set in motion, Baros sent you to the Stockade to find VanCleef's captive lieutenant, Bazil Thredd. But you arrived to find the prison in chaos, its cells thrown open and the guards fighting a desperate battle to contain the inmates. Now, Warden Thelwater has given you a grim ultimatum. You must descend into the riot, hunt down the treacherous lieutenant, and return with his severed head, or die alongside the rest of the prisoners in the dark."}},[302]={k="65",["end"]={d=166,t="You sought the truth behind the thugs driving the people from Westfall, tracing rumors from Lakeshire to Mathias Shaw in Stormwind. The mystery unraveled into a bitter truth. The men terrorizing the countryside were the very Stonemasons who rebuilt the capital, pushed to villainy by a kingdom's neglect. After intercepting their dispatches and escorting a terrified traitor through the wilds, you uncovered their hidden stronghold. Deep within, you assassinated their brilliant leader, Edwin VanCleef. By taking his head, you crippled his ruthless syndicate and sparked a glimmer of hope that peace might finally return to the plains."},before={a=166,t="You sought out Wiley the Black in Lakeshire to uncover who led the ruthless gang plaguing Westfall. The indebted rogue surrendered a hurried note detailing a strange alliance with gnolls, kobolds, and goblins. Gryan Stoutmantle caught a whispered mention of the Stonemasons within that missive. Seeking clarity, you ventured to Stormwind to consult Mathias Shaw of SI:7. He revealed that Edwin VanCleef, the talented architect who rebuilt the city after the First War, had turned to crime after a bitter dispute with the King. Stoutmantle demanded proof of this unthinkable betrayal. You intercepted a messenger on the dusty roads near Moonbrook, claiming a letter that confirmed VanCleef’s command. With the mastermind exposed, you escorted a captured traitor through hostile territory, fending off his former comrades until he revealed the gang's secret stronghold. Now, only one grim task remains. Though it is a heavy burden to condemn a man to death, VanCleef must be permanently silenced for the safety of the people, and his head delivered as proof."}},[11]={k="638",mid={d=641,t="Vol'jin demanded the legendary sword Trol'kalar for the coming war against Zul'Gurub, sending you to Arathi Highlands. The ancient blade lay locked away in the ruined city of Stromgarde, sealed within the tomb of Thoras Trollbane. To break the seals, you needed three sigils scattered among the city's scavengers and survivors. You carved through the Syndicate to rip the Sigil of Strom from their grasp. Then, you hunted down the Stromgarde militia, stripping eleven shattered fragments of the Sigil of Thoradin from their defenders. With the pieces in hand, the shaman Tor'gan forged them back into a whole, bringing you one step closer to the prize. Now, two keys are yours. Yet the final sigil remains hidden, carried by unknown hands shifting somewhere across the highlands, and the tomb stays sealed."},["end"]={d=646,t="You scoured the crumbling ruins of Stromgarde, tearing ancient sigils from the hands of thieves, cavalrymen, and a desperate human prince. With the shattered wards restored, you broke the seal upon the tomb of Thoras Trollbane. The stone hands surrendered their prize, and you claimed the legendary blade Trol'kalar. By delivering humanity's most feared weapon to Zengu, you have forever shifted the balance of power. The once mighty bloodline of Strom is broken, and the Darkspear now hold the key to conquering the steamy jungles of Zul'Gurub."}},[19]={k="991",["end"]={d=1046,t="You set out to find Teronis, only to discover his corpse among the murlocs. Taking up his unfinished work, you gathered the scattered pieces of Dartol's rod from corrupted treants and slaughtered druids. After reforging the artifact and awakening its magic at a hidden shrine, you used its power to walk among the furbolgs in disguise. You won the trust of an uncorrupted outcast named Krolg and struck down the vicious chieftain Ran Bloodtooth. By returning his severed skull to Raene Wolfrunner, you ensured Teronis did not die in vain and delivered a hard-won victory to the Sentinels."},mid={d=1027,t="You answered Raene Wolfrunner's plea to find her missing friend Teronis. At the shrine in Lake Falathim, you discovered his broken body, slain by the murlocs that claim the waters. Taking up his cause, you recovered his journal and the gem he sought. Following his notes, you found the dryad Shael'dryn at her moonwell. She guided you through Ashenvale to reforge Dartol's Rod, an evil wizard's creation that Teronis believed could slow the furbolg attacks. You battled twisted treants for a hidden chest near Felwood and scoured the ruins of Dor'Danil, where murdered druids once guarded the final fragment. Now, the pieces of the shattered rod lie gathered before Shael'dryn, but whether she can truly mend such dark magic remains unknown."}},[21]={k="1010",["end"]={d=1035,t="You journeyed through Ashenvale to save a stricken child, gathering every remedy Orendil Broadleaf could devise. From the Forsaken-infested ruins of Bathran's Haunt to the waters of Iris Lake, you sought herbs and the restorative magic of Elune's Tear. When these only slowed the sickness, you claimed frosted dust from the Ruins of Stardust to break her fever. Finally, you traveled to Fallen Sky Lake and slew the Shadethicket Oracle, prying a powerful moonstone from its grasp. By delivering this stone to Pelturas Whitemoon in Astranaar, you restored young Relara’s strength. A fragile life was spared, and a desperate father's hope was made whole."}},[22]={k="6382",["end"]={d=247,t="You traveled from the Barrens to test your might in the untamed wilderness of Ashenvale. At Splintertree Post, Senani Thunderheart challenged you to hunt three legendary creatures. You tracked the great bear Ursangous and the nightsaber Shadumbra through the dense forest, besting them both. Your final prey was the fierce hippogryph Sharptalon, a beast that frequently attacked the local peons. By striking down these powerful animals and claiming their trophies, you demonstrated remarkable strength. You proved yourself a true hunter, making the frontier safer for the Horde and ensuring songs of your bravery will be sung around the campfires."}},[23]={k="6564",["end"]={d=6565,t="You uncovered a damp, crumpled note detailing a sinister plot by the Twilight's Hammer to amass crystals radiating with water magic. These stones were intended to empower their aquamancers and placate Aku'Mai, all in a mad bid to restore the chaotic reign of the Old Gods. Bringing this grim discovery to Je'neu Sancrea revealed the orchestrator: Lorgus Jett. Venturing into the flooded halls of Blackfathom Deeps, you hunted Lorgus down and slew him. Returning victorious to Zoram'gar, you delivered the news. Your decisive strike shattered their dark ambition, ensuring the destructive forces of the Old Gods remain contained for now."},before={a=6565,t="You found a damp, crumpled note bearing poorly scrawled handwriting that detailed a sinister plot. It revealed that priestesses were gathering crystals brimming with the spirits of water elementals to empower aquamancers in their dark summonings. Their ultimate aim was to appease the entity known as Aku'Mai and usher in an era ruled by the ancient, chaotic Old Gods. Taking this troubling discovery to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar provided a name to the unseen enemy. He recognized the architect of these troubles as Lorgus Jett, a follower of the Twilight's Hammer. This cult, devoted to long-defeated creatures of chaos and destruction, holds no understanding of the spirits of nature. Realizing the severity of the threat and his own physical weakness, Je'neu Sancrea tasked you with stopping the cultist. Now, you must venture into the darkness of Blackfathom Deeps to find Lorgus Jett and end his life, returning to Zoram'gar only when the task is complete."}},[24]={k="1016",["end"]={d=1017,t="You gathered bracers from corrupted water elementals, harnessing them to focus a divining scroll. The scrying revealed the defiler: Sarilus Foulborne, an undead mage conjuring filth from Dreadmist Peak in the Barrens. Sickened by his deliberate destruction of the forest, Sentinel Velene Starstrike sent you into enemy territory. You scaled the peak and executed the miscreant, returning with his severed head to silence his arrogant laughter. Your decisive strike spared the sacred pools from further rot, proving to the Horde exactly what happens to those who earn the wrath of the Sentinels."}},[25]={k="25",["end"]={d=824,t="You cleared the Talondeep Path, cutting through the frenzied water elementals that had brought travel to a standstill at Mystral Lake. While scouting the gazebo overlooking the nearby Alliance outpost, you discovered a glowing, tainted globe among the elemental remains. Knowing this foul artifact held the key to the lake's madness, you brought it to Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post, who sent you to Zoram'gar Outpost. There, Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring recognized the defiled source of elemental power. He took the relic into his order's care, offering hope that this creeping corruption might finally be stopped."},before={a=824,t="You journeyed to Mystral Lake to break the dangerous standstill on the paths between Ashenvale and Stonetalon. By cutting down the raging water elementals, you secured the vital transport routes and successfully scouted a gazebo to spy on the nearby Alliance forces. Yet, in the bloody aftermath, you uncovered something far more sinister than a simple elemental uprising. From the shattered remains of a fallen creature, you retrieved an intensely glowing, corrupted globe of water. You carried the disgusting anomaly back to Splintertree Post, but Mastok Wrilehiss knew little of such strange afflictions. Knowing that the Earthen Ring preserves the elements and studies ancient legends, he sent you onward. Now, you make your way toward the coast of the Zoram Strand. You seek the Zoram'gar Outpost to find Je'neu Sancrea, bringing him the befouled globe in the hope that he can uncover its significance."}},[28]={k="1022",["end"]={d=1044,t="You sought the truth behind the howling wolf-men of Ashenvale. Your investigation began with a mysterious tome and a vanished priestess, Velinde Starsong. Following her trail carried you far across the ocean, sailing from Ratchet to the southern jungle, and onward to the perpetual gloom of Duskwood. There, you fought alongside the Carevin family against the fierce beasts Velinde had unwittingly unleashed. Deep within an overrun mine, you finally uncovered the priestess's grim end. You returned to the Sentinels bearing a heavy truth: Velinde had perished, leaving the powerful Scythe of Elune lost to her people."},mid={d=1039,t="You found the Tome of Mel'Thandris within a ruined shrine, surrounded by the haunting calls of savage wolf-men. Its pages revealed a strange vision of Priestess Velinde Starsong receiving a mysterious artifact known as the Scythe of Elune. Seeking answers, you learned she had vanished while battling the demonic presence in the northern forests. Using a key, you unlocked a heavy chest in the Sentinels' bunkhouse to examine her old journals. Her writings painted a troubling picture of her sudden departure, forcing you to track her path. Braving the hostile, sun-baked plains of the Barrens, you reached the bustling goblin port of Ratchet. Now you stand before the dockmaster and his dusty ledgers, waiting to see if she truly sailed for Blackwater Cove, and what mysterious fate ultimately befell her."}},[38]={k="861",["end"]={d=873,t="You left Mulgore to test your worth in the harsh expanse of the Barrens. From the Crossroads to Camp Taurajo, you honed your cunning against the beasts of the dry plains. You learned the honor of the wild by besting fierce legends like the elusive Echeyakee and the relentless Ishamuhale. After surviving the crushing footfalls of thunder lizards and the fury of thunderhawks, you faced the human-held coast. Plunging into the waters, you struck down Isha Awak, the Deep Doom. By claiming the heart of this mighty terror, you absorbed its solemn pride. You arrived as eager prey and forged yourself into an apex predator."},mid={d=881,t="Your journey on the hunter's path began in Mulgore, where Skorn Whitecloud recognized your wanderlust. After you proved your resolve against the flatland prowlers, Melor Stonehoof guided you to the Barrens to harden your spirit. At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn tested your mettle. You culled the nuisance plainstriders, gathered hooves from the sturdy zhevra, and finally tracked the deadly savannah prowlers through the tall grasses. Your growing strength earned you the right to challenge Echeyakee, the fiercest of the savannah cats. By sounding a horn among ancient kodo bones, you summoned Whitemist and claimed victory, carrying his merciful spirit with you. You have conquered the great white beast, but your path is far from over. What fresh prey waits for you in the dry plains, and what trials will Sergra demand you face next?"}},[39]={k="886",["end"]={d=914,t="You journeyed to the Barrens to trace a strange power seeping from the earth. Beneath the oases, you discovered fissures that breathed unnatural life into the wastes and twisted the beasts that drank there. Tracking this taint to Thunder Bluff, you learned its true source was the Druids of the Fang. Though they once sought to heal the land, this order lost its way in a dark slumber and tried to reshape the world into a nightmare. You descended into the Wailing Caverns, vanquished their four leaders, and claimed their dream gems. Through your triumph, the terrible visions shattered, and you saved the land from a cursed future."},before={a=1489,t="Sent by the druids of Thunder Bluff to the harsh plains of the Barrens, you met Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads to investigate a strange power leaking into the parched earth. At the Forgotten Pools, you discovered a bubbling fissure beneath the waters. Seeking to understand this phenomenon, you journeyed to the Stagnant Oasis and cast dead seeds into another fissure, only to watch impossible life spring from nothing. But this miraculous growth was unnatural. You hunted the snapjaws gathering at the oases and brought back their shells. They revealed a terrible taint that confused the land itself, leaving the soil caught in a waking dream. Now, it is clear that the Wailing Caverns are the true source of this corruption. But before you can delve into that dangerous place, you must return to the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. The elder druid Hamuul Runetotem awaits you there, ready to offer his wise counsel."}},[43]={k="887",["end"]={d=888,t="You struck out against the Southsea Freebooters plaguing the waters south of Ratchet, thinning their ranks of brigands and cannoneers. When Gazlowe suspected those same pirates of intercepting his trade fleet cargo, you brought his ledger to Wharfmaster Dizzywig to confirm the loss. Knowing the thieves held his property, you returned to the camp and fought through the pirates to reclaim what was stolen. You recovered a delicate telescopic lens needed to complete Gazlowe's observatory, along with his missing shipment of boots. By returning the goods, you dealt a blow to the pirates' raiding operation and proved your worth to the goblins of Ratchet."}},[44]={k="894A",["end"]={d=902,t="Sent to a Venture Company research facility near the Sludge Fen, you discovered a strange control console buzzing with erratic lights. You systematically shut off its valves, deactivating the machinery before prying the necessary key from Tinkerer Sniggles. Unlocking the console, you dug through a tangled mess of wires to rip the samophlange from its housing. You carried the mysterious device back to Sputtervalve in Ratchet. While its true function still eludes you, the Tinkers' Union in Undermine will soon dissect your prize to lay bare whatever secrets the Venture Company was so eager to hide."}},[45]={k="894H",["end"]={d=3924,t="You entered a Venture Company research site to pry an enigmatic device called a samophlange from its console. After shutting down the valves and claiming a key from Tinkerer Sniggles, you brought the prize to Sputtervalve. He promptly broke it. Seeking repairs, you hauled the contraption to Wenikee Boltbucket, scavenging nugget slugs to aid her work. When she failed, you carried the scrap to Rilli Greasygob in Orgrimmar. By hunting down Boss Copperplug and gathering his scattered manual pages, you delivered the knowledge required to mend the machine. The device finally rests in capable hands, though its true nature remains a mystery."},mid={d=902,t="Sent by Sputtervalve far to the north, southwest of the Sludge Fen, you hunted down a Venture Company research facility. Your quarry was a strange device known only as a samophlange. Relying on an operating manual, you breached their chaotic control console. You methodically shut off the fuel, regulator, and main control valves to deactivate the apparatus, but found the mechanism locked. You stripped the console key from Tinkerer Sniggles, drained the terminal's power, and plunged your hands into a tangled nest of wire to rip the samophlange from its housing. You carried the prize back to Ratchet, handing it to Sputtervalve for study before its journey to the Tinkers' Union in Undermine. Yet as he peered at the scavenged machinery, the true purpose of the samophlange remained a mystery."}},[48]={k="867",["end"]={d=1060,t="You answered Darsok Swiftdagger's call at the Crossroads, striking out to bleed the harpy threat dry. You started by culling the Witchwing flock in the northwest, then pushed into the Dry Hills to dismantle their command. When Darsok revealed that Serena Bloodfeather drove the attacks to avenge her fallen sister, you severed the matriarch's head, crushing her vendetta. Your violent work echoed beyond the Barrens. Carrying the news to Witch Doctor Jin'Zil in the caves of Malaka'Jin, you ended a bitter feud that began with Rexxar long ago. With the Bloodfeather lineage finally extinguished, the Horde caravans could travel safely once more."}},[49]={k="850",["end"]={d=4021,t="You hunted the Kolkar centaurs across the dry plains of the Barrens, cutting down their rising chieftains. One by one, you claimed the heads of Barak Kodobane, Verog the Dervish, and Hezrul Bloodmark, fracturing their leadership. Yet your victories provoked a desperate retaliation. A vengeful host marched from Desolace to assault the Horde bunkers. You met this invading tide head-on, shattering their ranks and felling Warlord Krom'zar. By tearing a scrap from his fallen banner, you extinguished the centaur invasion. You secured the land, ensuring that tales of your fierce defense would reach Thrall himself."}},[51]={k="865",["end"]={d=1491,t="You sought out the sunscale scytheclaws across the Barrens, harvesting their horns for Mebok Mizzyrix. He hoped to brew a concoction of pure intellect, but his first experiment failed. Undeterred, he sent you into the depths of the Wailing Caverns to extract Wailing Essence from ectoplasmic creatures. Mebok believed this strange substance caused the unnatural growth spreading through the land. You delivered the volatile essence into his eager hands so he could craft his new drink. Your part in his reckless scheme was finished, leaving him to chase his fortune."},before={a=1491,t="You hunted the sunscale scytheclaws roaming the sun-baked plains of the Barrens, harvesting their horns for an ambitious goblin in Ratchet. Mebok Mizzyrix believed these beasts possessed a unique cunning, and he planned to crush their crowns to brew beverages that would elevate the mind. He hoped to amass a vast wealth from the resulting elixir, but the strange concoction failed entirely to spark any newfound brilliance. Left grasping for a more potent ingredient, his attention shifted toward the unusual plants and animals spreading across the landscape. Mebok now suspects a mysterious substance known as Wailing Essence is the true source of these unnatural changes. Undeterred by his earlier failure, he has set you on a darker path to salvage his enterprise. Your journey leads west, away from the open skies and into the suffocating gloom of the Wailing Caverns. In those echoing tunnels, you must hunt the formless, ectoplasmic creatures that gather there, and harvest the shimmering essence they harbor."}},[57]={k="6562",["end"]={d=6563,t="Heeding Tsunaman's warning, you traveled far across the land to reach the Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale. There, you offered your aid to Je'neu Sancrea, who sent you down into the shadowed depths of Blackfathom Deeps. From the cavern walls, you pried glowing sapphires, striking against the naga who sought to hoard them. You delivered those precious stones safely to Je'neu, keeping their potent water magic out of enemy hands. Whatever dark arcane rituals the naga intended to fuel with that raw elemental power, you shattered their twisted schemes upon the shore."},before={a=6562,t="You answered the urgent call of Tsunaman, learning of a distant ally in desperate need of your aid. He asked you to seek out Je'neu Sancrea, who awaited assistance far away at the Zoram'gar Outpost. The path laid before you meant leaving familiar lands behind to plunge into the ancient, shadowed woods of Ashenvale, a vast night elf forest sprawling north of the rugged Stonetalon mountains. To reach the distant western shores of the Zoram Strand, you faced a demanding journey navigating the treacherous passes of Windshear Crag or traversing the sun-scorched expanse of the Barrens. It promised to be a long, arduous road leading deep into hostile and heavily contested territory where dangers lurked at every turn. Now, as you finally prepare to set out across the untamed wilderness toward the remote coastal outpost, a grave warning lingers in your mind. You must be careful upon the strand, for there are forces there that will not take to your presence kindly."}},[58]={k="1198",["end"]={d=1200,t="Dispatched by Dawnwatcher Shaedlass, you tracked the missing scout, Argent Guard Thaelrid, into the corrupted depths of Blackfathom Deeps along the coasts of Ashenvale. Finding him weakened, you uncovered the grim truth behind the alliance of the naga and the Twilight's Hammer. A servant of an Old God, Aku'Mai, had claimed a tainted Moon Well within the ancient temple of Elune. You struck down the cult's ruthless leader, Twilight Lord Kelris, putting an end to his horrific sacrifices. By carrying his severed head back to Dawnwatcher Selgorm in Darnassus, you halted a terrible evil and secured a quiet victory for the Argent Dawn."},before={a=1198,t="You met with Dawnwatcher Shaedlass, an agent of the Argent Dawn, to learn of the dark rumors whispering along the coasts of Ashenvale. The unholy union of the Twilight's Hammer and the sinister naga within Blackfathom Deeps had drawn the order's watchful eye. Seeking to gather knowledge on this spreading shadow, she had dispatched a brave scout into those treacherous caverns. But the weeks simply bled away, and Argent Guard Thaelrid never returned to give his vital report. With the rest of her forces scattered to face other pressing matters across the fractured land, the heavy burden of discovery fell squarely upon your shoulders. You listened intently as the weary Dawnwatcher recounted the long, agonizing silence of her missing operative. Now, you stand at the precipice of those watery, echoing halls, staring down into the damp dark. You must venture forth to seek out Argent Guard Thaelrid inside Blackfathom Deeps, and give him whatever aid he might require against the gathered darkness."}},[59]={k="6344",["end"]={d=6343,t="You answered a call in Darnassus and sought out Nessa Shadowsong in Rut'theran Village. Tasked as her courier, you flew a peculiar collection of oversized fish bones across the sea to Laird in Auberdine. His shock at their massive scale confirmed a strange truth: the sea life clinging to Teldrassil was growing far larger than anything found along the mainland coast. You returned to Nessa with Laird's suspicion that the great tree itself might be warping the nearby wildlife. Though the true cause remained hidden, the villagers were left content to harvest the uncanny riches the waters provided."}},[60]={k="983",["end"]={d=1003,t="You set out to aid Wizbang Cranktoggle with his communication inventions, the Buzzboxes spread around Auberdine. Scouring the wilds, you gathered beast parts to feed the clanking contraptions. Yet with every repair, the distant voice over the crackling transmission grew thicker, his speech more slurred. Ultimately, his true design revealed itself. You were never maintaining relays at all. Instead, your tireless labor supplied a hidden illicit brewing operation right beneath the noses of the nightelves, distilling the very liquor that fueled his drunken revelry."}},[61]={k="954",["end"]={d=957,t="Sent by Thundris Windweaver to the ruins of Bashal'Aran, you sought the source of a blue aura avoided by demons. There you found the spectral Asterion, trapped in eternal torment. To break his prison, you hunted grells and their satyr masters, claiming the ancient seal that bound him. Plunging it into the blue flames of Ameth'Aran, you shattered his chains. Asterion walks the forests freely for the first time since the reign of Queen Azshara. Yet his release brings a chilling realization. He senses his ancient jailor, Athrikus, still lives, and the spirit's long despair has kindled into a burning desire for vengeance."}},[64]={k="4811",["end"]={d=4813,t="You ventured east of Auberdine, seeking a strange red crystal that was drawing hostile moonkin to the mountains. Finding the anomaly, you washed it in pure moonwell water at the behest of Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea. The potent magic cleared the crystal's opaque surface, exposing a grim sight trapped within its impenetrable lattice: shattered bones and a humanoid jaw. You carried this dark revelation back to Auberdine for the council's judgment. Whatever foul influence creeps down from Felwood to twist the moonkin, its source remains locked within that crimson stone, a silent threat looming over the distant eastern ridge."}},[65]={k="730",["end"]={d=943,t="You sought Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker's crew in Darkshore, finding Archaeologist Hollee terrified for Prospector Remtravel. Venturing south, you guarded the oblivious prospector from horrible golems until he unearthed a mysterious fossil. Returning this artifact to Darnassus, you learned of a matching discovery across the sea. You sailed to Menethil Harbor to find Archaeologist Flagongut, then hunted through the Wetlands to recover his swallowed relic from savage raptors and retrieved the original fossil from Prospector Whelgar. With the Stone of Relu and both fossils finally brought together, the eager scholar began deciphering the forgotten powers locked within the ancient rock."}},[66]={k="984",["end"]={d=990,t="You investigated the taint spreading through Darkshore, discovering the Blackwood furbolgs had already succumbed to the madness. After thinning their ranks to safeguard Auberdine, you gathered moonstalker pelts so Terenthis could craft a magical cloak. Hidden by its illusion, you followed Grimclaw past the corrupted beasts to find Volcor wounded in a cave. You fought your way out at his side, carving a path back to the safety of the road. Your victories brought hope to Auberdine and proved your strength. Because of this, Sentinel Selarin sent you south to Astranaar, bringing much-needed aid to Raene Wolfrunner against the corruption gripping Ashenvale."}},[67]={k="947",["end"]={d=951,t="You ventured behind Cliffspring Falls to gather fungi for Barithras Moonshade, uncovering a sinister presence. The Ancient Onu then guided you to the Master's Glaive, where you discovered the Twilight's Hammer cult seeking the residual power of a fallen lord. Scouring their camp, you barely escaped the maddening grip of a twisted tome, tearing away a single cursed page. In its chaotic scrawls, Onu saw the cult's true design: to use elven magic to revive their ancient masters. By unearthing faded relics from the ruins of Mathystra, you secured the key to understanding how they plan to exploit this power."}},[68]={k="965",mid={d=970,t="You left Auberdine to find a missing scout, Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze fearing the worst. Near the Tower of Althalaxx, you discovered Balthule Shadowstrike watching warlocks gather outside its walls. From the soiled parchments you stripped from their bodies, a name surfaced: the Cult of the Dark Strand. Carrying his hurried warning, you journeyed south to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale Forest to find the paladin Delgren the Purifier. Recognizing the threat, he sent you to strike at the cultists in Ordil'Aran and seize a corrupted relic. You returned bearing a glowing soul gem that pulsed with dark magic. Delgren now studies the stone's enchantments, but the secret of the cult's power—and whatever evil lies trapped inside the gem—remains entirely unknown."},["end"]={d=981,t="You sought Balthule Shadowstrike in Darkshore and stumbled upon warlocks gathering at the Tower of Althalaxx. Carrying their foul parchments south into Ashenvale, you allied with Delgren the Purifier to dismantle the Cult of the Dark Strand. You shattered their captured soul gems, executed the orc warlock Ilkrud Magthrull, and purged their satyr-held camps. Returning to the lightning-struck tower, you scaled its heights and struck down the cult's leader, Athrikus Narassin. His death scattered the cult and broke their demonic grip. The forests are safe once more, and the paladin has offered his blessing in gratitude for your deeds."}},[70]={k="2098",["end"]={d=2078,t="When threshadons sank Gelkak Gyromast's ship off Darkshore, the pirate lost both his vessel and his first mate. The key to reactivate his mechanical crewman shattered on the rocks, its fragments swallowed by raging crawlers, ferocious foreststriders, and murlocs. You hunted the hostile beasts to reclaim the missing pieces. With the tool restored, you tracked down the stranded companion, powered him up, and brought him back to exact revenge on the local murloc chief. The sea swallowed a pirate ship, but you reunited a captain with his metal friend and earned his salty respect."}},[77]={k="1437",["end"]={d=1440,t="You found an unsent letter and brought it to Baros Alexston, uncovering a hidden threat. He sent you to Mathias Shaw, who revealed that the riots inside the prison were being commanded by a captive named Bazil Thredd. After speaking with Warden Thelwater, you plunged into the violent cellblocks. You carved a path through the raging inmates, tracked down Thredd, and ended his life. With his defeat, the rebellion was shattered. By severing the head of the uprising, you extinguished a dangerous plot that had been secretly festering in the very heart of the city."}},[78]={k="1453",["end"]={d=1467,t="You left the Stonetalon Mountains behind and traveled into the bleak wastes of Desolace to find employment. Following Roetten Stonehammer's advice, you navigated the northern peaks to locate a secluded refuge called Nijel's Point. Inside this quiet outpost, you met Kreldig Ungor and offered your services to the Reclaimers. Your journey proved worthwhile, cementing your place within their ranks. In a troubled land where folk often lose cherished relics or their own kin, you threw in your lot with a band willing to recover anything, provided the coin is good."}},[84]={k="182",["end"]={d=420,t="You answered Grelin Whitebeard's call to thin out the trolls occupying a cave in Coldridge Valley. When a brute stole his journal, you ventured into the frost to reclaim it. With the immediate threat handled and his report finished, Grelin trusted you to carry his findings to his brother. You braved a tunnel swarming with savage troggs to reach Kharanos and deliver the missive. Now, Senir Whitebeard has the document in hand. Though Grelin's lack of tact might offend the Senate, the truth of the dangers lurking in the snow is finally bound for Ironforge."}},[92]={k="96392",["end"]={d=96393,t="You met with Earthseer Farsen in Dun Morogh, who showed you a grim vision of Dark Iron dwarves gathering. Acting on his warning, you struck at their spies near Ironband's Compound. Among their belongings, you discovered a map detailing hidden tunnels converging beneath Ironforge itself. Pressing into the cavernous depths of Old Ironforge, you fought your way through the Hall of Thanes and slew their commander, Durgen Dirgehammer. By delivering his head to King Magni Bronzebeard, you exposed the subterranean invasion. With the dwarven capital spared from disaster, the king's guards moved to seal the breaches and secure the lower vaults."}},[93]={k="96408",["end"]={d=96393,t="Sent to investigate a lonely campfire above Gol'Bolar Quarry, you met Earthseer Farsen. He showed you the creeping threat of Dark Iron spies infesting Dun Morogh. After you slaughtered the scouts at Ironband's Compound, you found a map detailing a far more sinister plot. Its jagged runes revealed hidden tunnels converging directly beneath Ironforge. Descending into the Hall of Thanes beneath the ancient city, you struck down the invasion's commander, Durgen Dirgehammer. By delivering his severed head to King Magni Bronzebeard, you exposed the unseen enemy. The royal guards will now seal the cavernous breaches, securing the dwarven capital against the darkness below."}},[94]={k="637",["end"]={d=700,t="You pulled a waterlogged envelope from the icy depths, delivering its final words to Sara Balloo. Carrying her sorrowful plea to Ironforge, you found King Magni Bronzebeard heavily burdened by the sacrifices of his people. Unable to return her husband from the Twisting Nether, the monarch resolved to honor him in stone. You journeyed to Darrow Hill in Hillsbrad, hauling fine Alterac Granite from the ruins of Lordaeron. With this material, Grand Mason Marblesten chiseled a lasting tribute. While no monument can replace a lost life, it now stands to remind future generations of brave soldiers like Sully Balloo who gave everything for the Alliance."}},[95]={k="792",["end"]={d=924,t="You uncovered a dark taint in the Valley of Trials, striking down familiars and claiming a medallion from the Burning Blade. Hunting their agents across Durotar, you slew the warlock Fizzle Darkstorm and gathered searing collars from the cultists inside Skull Rock. The demonic trail led through Orgrimmar to the Barrens, where you carried a volatile power stone high atop Dreadmist Peak. There, at a fiery altar, you shattered the Demon Seed. You severed the cult's connection to the Burning Legion, yet its destruction sent a shockwave through the unseen world. Durotar is safe for now, but hidden forces surely know you broke their prize."},mid={d=806,t="You began in the Valley of Trials under the guidance of Zureetha Fargaze, who sensed a dark taint. In a nearby cave, you struck at a coven of the Burning Blade, slaying their Vile Familiars and retrieving the Burning Blade Medallion pulsing with black magic. Fearing this was merely a herald, you carried word of the cult to Sen'jin Village. Master Gadrin revealed that while his home was safe, their dark influence had already taken root across the waters of the Echo Isles. Journeying to Razor Hill, you warned Orgnil Soulscar of the rising threat. His investigations directed you to Thunder Ridge, where you tracked down and slew the goblin warlock Fizzle Darkstorm, returning with his severed claw. You struck a heavy blow, yet the true depth of the cult's reach remains unknown."}},[97]={k="5",["end"]={d=240,t="You found Jitters hiding in a ghost town, desperate for a decent meal after weeks of eating weeds. Knowing he craved Dusky Crab Cakes from the Scarlet Raven Tavern, you traveled to Darkshire to meet Chef Grual. The cook revealed his grim secret: the famous cakes were actually made from Venom Web Spiders. You hunted the creatures in the northern foothills, harvesting their gooey legs. Once Grual fried the strange meat with his hidden spices, you brought the steaming dish back to the ruined town. Delivering the disguised meal to Jitters finally sated his hunger, offering the terrified man a small comfort in the darkness."}},[98]={k="164",["end"]={d=55,t="You tracked a shadowy witness across Duskwood and uncovered a tragic tale of murder by the Dark Riders. The trail ended with a terrified man named Jitters and a journal exposing the necromancer Morbent Fel. To pierce the wizard's protective magic, you recovered Lightforge Iron from a sunken ship in the Wetlands and had it forged into a blessed weapon in Stormwind. Wielding this holy steel, you stormed Morbent Fel's lair overlooking the Raven Hill cemetery and struck him down. Though the Dark Riders remain at large, you delivered vengeance for Sven Yorgen and struck a mighty blow against the evils plaguing the land."},mid={d=268,t="You brought supplies to Sven Yorgen's camp in Duskwood and learned of a terrible tragedy: Dark Riders from Deadwind Pass had slaughtered his family. At his abandoned farm, you unearthed a dirt-stained journal buried by a shadowy figure who witnessed the massacre. Tracking the book's origins through Darkshire, you questioned Madame Eva, Clerk Daltry, and Tavernkeep Smitts. They recalled a terrified stranger fleeing west toward Raven Hill. You hunted him down and found Jitters, the journal's nervous author. Afraid of Sven's wrath, Jitters handed over his completed journal instead of facing him. From its pages, Sven uncovered a vital lead: the murderous Dark Riders have been speaking with the wizard Morbent Fel at the Forlorn Rowe. What these phantom riders want, and what role the dark wizard plays in their schemes, is still unknown."}},[99]={k="165",mid={d=156,t="Elaine Carevin sent you to check on an old man living near the Raven Hill cemetery. You found Abercrombie isolated in his shack, unable to navigate the dangerous roads. Eager to help the frail hermit, you ran his errands in Darkshire. To acquire Ghost Hair Thread, Madame Eva sent you to the tragic spirit Blind Mary. You gathered the hair with a spectral comb despite the weeping ghost's sudden horror at her monstrous state. Abercrombie was delighted with the strange thread, but immediately asked for Zombie Juice to warm his blood. Tavernkeep Smitts required rot blossoms to brew the strong liquor, sending you to harvest them from the skulls of roaming skeletons. You have gathered the macabre ingredients, but the hermit's true purpose for these sinister supplies remains entirely unknown."},["end"]={d=253,t="You brought an old hermit named Abercrombie thread spun from ghost hair, strong liquor brewed from rot blossoms, and the ribs of fallen ghouls. He claimed they were simple favors, but your kindness unwittingly aided a madman. When Sirra Von'Indi translated the hermit's ancient letter for the mayor, the horrible truth emerged: Abercrombie was the legendary Embalmer, plotting to unleash doom upon Darkshire. To undo your terrible mistake, you sought out the grave of his wife, Eliza. By tearing the Embalmer's own beating heart from her cursed chest, you broke his dark magic and secured a powerful defense for the town."}},[101]={k="174",["end"]={d=181,t="You supplied a simple bronze tube to Viktori Prism'Antras in Darkshire, the foundation of a bizarre contraption meant to pierce the heavens. Needing a polished surface to catch the light, you sought out Blind Mary, ultimately wrestling her abandoned looking glass from a roaming Insane Ghoul in the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery. For the final, massive lens, you descended into the ogre mound of southern Duskwood and struck down Zzarc'Vul to claim his monocle. Now, the completed device stands ready. Viktori turns his gaze to the distant stars, searching for truths beyond mere magic to explain the creeping blight upon the forest."}},[102]={k="173",["end"]={d=223,t="Seeking to join Master Carevin's cause in Darkshire, you ventured into the woods to prove your worth. You struck down the Nightbane Shadow Weavers in Brightwood Grove, then faced the brutal Dark Runners overrunning the Rotting Orchard. Despite your victories, the worgen seemed inexhaustible, drawn by an unknown dark power. Pressing south, you fought the deadly Vile Fangs and Tainted Ones near their bonfires and caves. Your relentless efforts earned Calor's respect and his official recommendation. Presenting it to Master Carevin, you were welcomed into his crusade. The harrowing trials forged you into a trusted weapon against the demons and undead threatening the realm."}},[103]={k="66",["end"]={d=98,t="A chilling vision set you on the trail of a phantom. You scoured registries in Darkshire, sifted through an abandoned schoolhouse in Moonbrook, and unearthed forgotten letters in a Goldshire inn. You pieced together the shredded journal pages from a butchered family's estate, matching the handwriting to a killer. It proved Stalvan Mistmantle was a monster responsible for a gruesome slaughter. You marched into the woods, faced the lunatic at his cottage, and ended his depraved life. Returning his family ring to Madame Eva brought a wave of hope, finally freeing Duskwood from his bloodthirst."},mid={d=72,t="A dark omen set you on this path. The mystic, Madame Eva, felt an unnatural chill in her veins and saw death waiting for her granddaughter, Alyssa. She gave you only a name: Stalvan. Your search began with Clerk Daltry and the town records, pointing you to an abandoned schoolhouse in Moonbrook, where an unsent letter lay gathering dust in an old footlocker. The trail then led to Innkeeper Farley in Goldshire, where you learned of a terrified messenger fleeing into a storm, leaving behind correspondence bound for the Canal District in Stormwind. Following that lead, you met Caretaker Folsom, a man haunted by the memory of a gruesome massacre. You opened a sealed crate of forgotten heirlooms, hoping for answers. Yet, the true identity of Stalvan Mistmantle, and the horror he unleashed, remain unknown."}},[119]={k="123",["end"]={d=147,t="You discovered a schedule detailing secret gold shipments from the mines of Elwynn Forest, bound for someone known as The Collector. Bringing this evidence to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire, you were sent to the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch to serve justice. You struck down the thief and claimed his ring, ending his theft from the kingdom. Yet this victory only unearthed a stranger truth. The trinket you recovered was a membership ring for the old Stonemason's Guild in Stormwind. The Defias Thieves are siphoning wealth from the realm's own mines, leaving troubling questions about what they intend to do with it."}},[120]={k="40",["end"]={d=59,t="You carried a merchant's warnings of murlocs to Goldshire, but it took grim proof to move Marshal Dughan. At the eastern bridge, you learned guards Rolf and Malakai had vanished. Following webbed footprints to Stone Cairn Lake, you uncovered their grisly fate. You retrieved their medallions from the half-eaten corpses, proving the creatures were more than a mere nuisance. Your report laid bare a grave threat to Elwynn Forest. Defenses were already stretched thin, and the loss of those men struck a heavy blow. Still, equipped with fresh armor from the Eastvale Logging Camp, you stood ready to defend the besieged woods."}},[121]={k="94",["end"]={d=249,t="You acted as the eyes of Theocritus, carrying his glyphs into dangerous territory to spy on his rival. First, you planted his magic upon an old lion statue near the Tower of Ilgalar, revealing a conflict between Morganth and the orcs. Pressing further, you hid another glyph within an empty jar at Stonewatch Keep. Through your efforts, Theocritus uncovered a terrifying truth: the warlock sought the Scythe of Elune. Rather than wait for disaster, you stormed the tower, struck Morganth down, and claimed his Pendant of Shadow. With the dark mage slain, the kingdom of Stormwind was spared from certain ruin."}},[123]={k="62",["end"]={d=11,t="You answered Marshal Dughan's call in Goldshire, delving into the dim tunnels of the Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines to uncover a spreading infestation of kobolds. With local forces stretched thin by the threat, you traveled west to the embattled Westbrook Garrison. There, you found Deputy Rainer desperate for capable hands. Brutish Riverpaw gnolls had overrun the woods and lake shores, pressing against the borders of Elwynn Forest. You waded into their ranks, striking them down and claiming their painted armbands as proof of your grim work. Your efforts bought the defenders precious time, holding the line against the encroaching wilds."}},[124]={k="85",["end"]={d=87,t="You searched for Bernice Stonefield's missing necklace, only to find yourself hunting boars to barter a pie for the memories of a hungry boy. Billy Maclure eventually confessed to losing the heirloom near the Fargodeep Mine, where a hulking kobold named Goldtooth snatched it up. Venturing into the earth, you tore the treasure from the creature's grasp. Handing back the jewelry brought tears to an old widow, earning you a small token of her fallen husband's luck. What started as a petty squabble between neighbors finished in a quiet victory, returning a piece of cherished history to a grieving soul."}},[144]={k="2923",["end"]={d=2922,t="You heard from Brother Sarno that Tinkmaster Overspark needed help. You found the tinkerer in Ironforge, mourning the fate of his mechanical assistant. When Gnomeregan fell, a jolt scrambled Techbot's positronic brain, turning the once-helpful machine into a frenzied hazard roaming the lost city's depths. Venturing into those ruined halls, you put an end to the rogue machine's rampage and salvaged its memory core. Returning the core safely to Overspark's hands, you preserved a vital piece of gnomish ingenuity, giving the tinkerer the chance to unravel the malfunction and one day restore his cherished creation."},before={a=2923,t="You listened as Brother Sarno shared the unfortunate tale of Techbot, a mechanical marvel built by the gnomes. Once, this clever automaton served as a kind and dependable helper, a testament to the ingenuity of its creators. Yet, word arrived that the machine had somehow broken down, its gears and logic twisting into sudden malfunction. Its creator, Tinkmaster Overspark, was deeply troubled by the grim fate of his prized invention, mourning what his creation had become. Sarno believed there was still a chance to set things right, holding onto the quiet hope that the broken machine could be repaired and returned to its former purpose. With this possibility in mind, you were sent out to offer your assistance. Now, your path leads into the heart of the great dwarven mountain. You must make your way through the grand halls of Ironforge and enter Tinker Town to find Tinkmaster Overspark, as the brilliant engineer would surely welcome your help to salvage his ruined masterpiece."}},[145]={k="2927",["end"]={d=2962,t="Moved by Gnoarn's grief over his lost hair and the tragic fall of Gnomeregan, you traveled to Kharanos to aid Ozzie Togglevolt. Desperate for a cure to the radiation sickness, Ozzie sent you into the infested city to harvest fallout from the irradiated troggs. When that weak sample proved useless, you plunged back into the toxic ruin, risking life and limb to extract volatile slime directly from the horrors wandering the halls. You returned carrying a vial of pure, concentrated ruin. With this dangerous substance secured, Ozzie finally has what he needs to test his formula, holding the fragile hope of saving the afflicted."},before={a=2927,t="You stood before a grieving gnome named Gnoarn, listening to a tale of profound loss. His sorrow was not just for the fall of a great marvel of engineering, but for the tragic ruin of his own magnificent hair, stripped away by the toxic fallout of his people's desperate defense. The radiation that seeped through the metallic halls of Gnomeregan claimed the only gnomefro in all of Azeroth, a tragedy he blamed entirely on the invasion of the filthy, relentless troggs. He shook his fist at the memory, carrying the bitter sting of a catastrophe that drove the brilliant tinkerers from their ancestral homes. Yet, in the shadow of that ruin, a faint glimmer of hope remained. A chance to undo the damage and perhaps even reclaim the lost capital still lingered in the frozen peaks. Now, you must seek out Ozzie Togglevolt and his partner Razzle in the settlement of Kharanos, where the two are tirelessly developing a method to save their irradiated city."}},[146]={k="2931",["end"]={d=2930,t="You answered Gaxim Rustfizzle's call and sought out Master Mechanic Castpipe in Ironforge. The gnomes had fled their great city of Gnomeregan, leaving behind a wealth of irreplaceable knowledge. Venturing deep into the irradiated ruin, you hunted down scattered security punch cards, steadily upgrading your clearance across a series of abandoned terminals. Finally reaching the high-security Matrix Punchograph 3005-D, you extracted the ultimate prize: the prismatic punch card. By returning this lost data to the surface, you restored a vital piece of gnomic ingenuity. It is a bold victory against the tragedy that befell their home, ensuring their brilliance survives."},before={a=2931,t="You listened to the earnest plea of Gaxim Rustfizzle, a proud member of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences. He told you of an urgent summons echoing from the distant mountain stronghold of Ironforge. Master Mechanic Castpipe is seeking brave souls willing to step directly into harm's way. Though Castpipe lacks the formal credentials of Gaxim's prestigious society, his intellect remains sharp and unquestioned. Gaxim ran the calculations, and the resulting odds painted a stark picture: this call truly matters. It is a grave situation you cannot afford to ignore. Now, you prepare to answer that summons. Castpipe is steadily gathering capable bands for a perilous and secretive undertaking. Your path leads you to join his ranks in Ironforge before plunging back into the treacherous depths of Gnomeregan. You are bound for a mission to retrieve critical data from the fallen gnome city, an operation shrouded in the absolute highest security and importance."}},[147]={k="2925",["end"]={d=2924,t="Mathiel shared the urgent plea of a dear friend, Klockmort Spannerspan, who sought aid for a dangerous expedition into Gnomeregan. You took up the burden, journeying to Ironforge and descending into the contaminated, maddened halls of the lost gnomish capital. Deep within the ruins, you forced open the artificial extrapolators left behind during the frantic exodus, salvaging the essential artificials inside. Returning with the hard-won mechanical components, you delivered them to Klockmort. Your perilous journey through the madness achieved far more than recovering forgotten scrap. By placing these vital tools back into capable hands, you sparked a grand leap forward in gnomish research and experimentation."},before={a=2925,t="You answered the call of Mathiel, hearing his tale of a distant friend in desperate need. Word had traveled far across the lands, carrying an urgent message from the gnome Klockmort Spannerspan. Though Mathiel deeply yearned to rush to his companion's side, his binding obligations forced him to remain behind. With a heavy heart, he pleaded for you to undertake the arduous journey in his stead, a favor for which he would be forever grateful. Having accepted this solemn burden, you made your way toward the towering dwarven gates of Ironforge to seek out Tinkertown. There, you prepare to find Klockmort and join his desperate cause. A grueling challenge lies ahead. You must soon embark on a profoundly perilous yet absolutely vital expedition into the depths of Gnomeregan. Once a great marvel of gnomish engineering, that magnificent metropolis is now hopelessly contaminated, its twisting iron halls entirely overrun by maddened gnomes and their erratic, corrupted mechanical creations."}},[148]={k="2945A",["end"]={d=2948,t="You pulled a filth-caked ring from the corpse of a Dark Iron dwarf. Sensing magic beneath the grime, you placed the band inside a Sparklematic 5200. The clanking machine scrubbed away the dirt, revealing the seal of Ironforge and three engraved initials. Tracing those letters led you to Talvash del Kissel. He recognized the trinket as his own work, left behind when Gnomeregan fell. Though he considered its presence in Dark Iron hands a troubling mystery, the gnome focused on his craft. For a modest fee, a bar of silver, and a moss agate, he reshaped his old creation into a finer ring for you to wear."},before={a=2945,t="You struck down the Dark Iron dwarves, their broken forms left scattered upon the unforgiving earth. Amidst the slaughter, a single prize caught your eye. Plucked from the corpse of a fallen foe, you discovered a simple band, utterly choked by thick layers of filth and caked mud. It was entirely unwearable in such a ruined state, the hardened residue clinging stubbornly to the rough surface. Yet, beneath the stifling grime, a faint luster called to you. A glimmer of precious metal hinted at fine craftsmanship, and the unmistakable glint of a hidden gem sparkled softly through the dark crust. These dwarves carried heavy secrets, and this crude trinket held mysteries of its own, locked tightly away beneath its thick shell of dirt. The true nature of this Grime-Encrusted Ring remains unknown, a stubborn mystery that resists your touch. If you are ever to make use of it, you must find something to strip the hardened residue away."}},[149]={k="2945H",["end"]={d=2950,t="You pried a grime-encrusted ring from the corpse of a Dark Iron dwarf. After you fed a coin into the Sparklematic 5200, the violently shaking machine churned out a shiny, gift-wrapped band bearing the seal of Orgrimmar. This clue led you to Nogg. He denied ownership but realized the Dark Irons having the jewelry meant gnomes likely stole their golem designs. Grateful for your intelligence about this brewing conflict, Nogg took your silver and agate to forge a stronger lattice for the ring. A simple piece of dirty salvage became a potent artifact, exposing a bitter rivalry between cunning inventors."},before={a=2945,t="You stood over the fallen body of a Dark Iron dwarf, the air choked with the dust of battle. As you searched the corpse, your fingers found something small and unyielding hidden within the soot-stained garments. It was a ring, though its true shape lay concealed beneath thick layers of baked dirt and hardened residue. The grime was caked on so thickly that slipping it onto your hand was completely impossible, yet its dense weight gave you pause. Peering closely through the filth, you caught the faint luster of precious metal and the unmistakable glint of a gemstone buried beneath the crust. You turned the heavy band over in your palm, wondering what secrets it held and how it came to be in such dark hands. But until it is cleansed, it remains utterly useless. If you are ever going to make use of this ring, you will first need to find something capable of washing the hardened residue away."}},[150]={k="2951",["end"]={d=2952,t="Amidst gnomes holding out against the madness, you discovered a strange contraption called the Sparklematic 5200. Hoping to salvage a filthy object, you surrendered three silver coins and your encrusted prize to the device. The metal beast lurched and roared in a violent frenzy, its frame groaning as it fought to strip away the heavy filth. The terrifying racket ceased with a sudden chime, and the machine opened to offer your item neatly wrapped in a little bow. You paid your silver to scour away the grime, but the device hid its handiwork inside a pretty package. The truth of your treasure now waits beneath that wrapping."},before={a=2951,t="You discovered a small group of desperate gnomes huddled together, holding out against the unrelenting madness that raged just outside their room. Standing out among these terrified survivors, you found a rather unusual contraption waiting in the gloom. A small metal plaque mounted to its heavy casing clearly identified the strange machine as The Sparklematic 5200. The device offered a mechanical remedy for the thick dirt caked onto your equipment, claiming it could restore the luster to your belongings. It required nothing more than a toll of three silver coins deposited into its slot and a brief wait for its internal mechanisms to process the payment. Now, standing before this bizarre piece of engineering amidst the chaos of the survivors' refuge, you pull the tarnished scrap from your heavy bags. You prepare to insert your grime-covered trinkets into the mechanism, drop your hard-earned silver into the coin slot, and give the contraption a moment to operate so your valuables might emerge spotless."}},[153]={k="527",["end"]={d=550,t="You systematically dismantled the human presence in Hillsbrad, starting with the farmers in their fields and the terrified peasants hiding in the orchards. You severed their supply lines by executing Blacksmith Verringtan and seized the town registry to uncover the Azureload Mine, slaughtering the workers within. You crushed their leadership by assassinating Magistrate Burnside and storming the dwarven stronghold of Dun Garok, leaving Captain Ironhill dead. Returning to the Undercity, you brought word of your ruthless victories to Varimathras. Your relentless campaign proved to the high command that the humans could fall, clearing the path to face the Scourge."}},[154]={k="509",["end"]={d=524,t="You scoured the fields for noxious blossoms and journeyed to the Undercity, where Master Apothecary Faranell added his rotting touch to your prize. Returning to Apothecary Lydon with more reagents in hand, you helped brew a horrific new plague. To test this vile elixir, you stole a keg of Shindigger Stout from the dwarves of Dun Garok, spiked it with the grim mixture, and left it for a group of captive human farmers. The tainted brew resting on the dusty rug sealed their gruesome fate, marking a cruel triumph for the Dark Lady."}},[155]={k="536",["end"]={d=563,t="You did the dirty work for a lazy guard desperate to leave his post. Lieutenant Farren Orinelle could barely stand the smell of Southshore, let alone fight the murlocs and naga threatening the town. Instead, you waded through the surf, slaughtering the beasts and hauling back their severed heads to satisfy Marshal Redpath. When the call came to deal with the naga, you struck them down too, all so Orinelle could claim the glory. You delivered his report to Major Samuelson in Stormwind. The coastal threat is thinned, and a cowardly lieutenant might finally secure the transfer he always wanted."}},[169]={k="6387",["end"]={d=6392,t="You bore a list of promising mining students from Brock Stoneseeker in Thelsamar across the snowy peaks to Ironforge. The gryphon master Thorgrum Borrelson provided the wings for your journey to the Great Forge District, where Golnir Bouldertoe received the names and chiseled them into a fresh batch of honorary picks. With the newly minted tools in hand, you took to the skies once more, riding one of Gryth Thurden's beasts back to Loch Modan. Your efforts ensured that a new generation of dwarven miners could finally begin their trade, ready to strike the rich ore deposits of the region with pride."}},[171]={k="2041",["end"]={d=2040,t="You sought out Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind, the commander of an assault crew preparing to reclaim Gnomeregan from the troggs. Her gyrodrillmatic excavationators lacked the energy to pierce the city's rocky borders. Venturing deep into the Deadmines, you recovered an intact power supply, the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket, from a functional goblin shredder. You delivered this vital machinery back to Shoni. Because of your efforts in those dark depths, the gnomes now possess the power to fuel their machines and breach the walls. You have paved the way for a fierce offensive to liberate their fallen home."},before={a=2040,t="You answered a call to help the gnomes reclaim their lost city from the vicious troggs. To join the battle for Gnomeregan, you traveled to Stormwind and found Shoni the Shilent, the commander of the underground assault crew. She explained that her mighty gyrodrillmatic excavationators were ready to carve through the earth, but they lacked the immense energy required to smash through the subterranean stone walls defending the ruined capital. To fuel her engines and pave the way for a massive counterattack, Shoni sent you on a perilous mission. Now, you must descend deep into the dangerous shafts of the Deadmines to hunt down a working goblin shredder. If you can dismantle the machine and secure its untouched power source, the great drills will finally have the strength to pierce the rocky perimeter, allowing the gnomish forces to pour through the breach and take back their home."}},[174]={k="224",["end"]={d=217,t="While King Magni's soldiers bled on distant battlefields, you stood resolute in Loch Modan. As a savage trogg infestation threatened to overwhelm Ironforge, you held the fragile front lines. You steadily thinned the relentless Stonesplinter forces, buying the embattled mountaineers critical time. When word came that no reinforcements would follow, you did not waver against the encroaching swarm. Striking at the heart of the incursion, you assassinated Chieftain Grawmug and his towering guards, Gnasher and Brawler. With their leadership broken, the brutal invasion collapsed, ensuring the safety of the dwarven lands."}},[176]={k="298",["end"]={d=309,t="You carried a simple request for blastpowder from Prospector Ironband to Thelsamar, and on to Prospector Stormpike in Ironforge. A troubling truth soon emerged: previous shipments had vanished without a trace. Hurrying back to check on the latest delivery, you found the porters under attack by their own companion. The missing powder was no accident. Dark Iron sympathizers like Saean had infiltrated the crew itself to steal supplies. You drove the ambushers off, guarded Miran on the road, and saw the remaining barrels safely to the excavation. Ironband finally has his powder, but a chilling reality remains: traitors hide among the dwarves."}},[178]={k="250",["end"]={d=283,t="You found strange powder near the Stonewrought Dam, uncovering a deadly plot. Recognizing the threat, you braved a perilous road to Dun Modr, where an explosives expert identified the substance as volatile Seaforium. To defuse it, you hunted venomous spiders, gathered tears from crocolisks, and wrested rare crystals from ogres. With the neutralizing mixture prepared, you dove to the base of the dam, pouring the compound into a planted keg just before it could detonate. The explosives fizzled, and the massive stone structure held firm. Through your swift actions, a devastating strike by the Dark Iron insurgents was thwarted, and the Stonewrought Dam remains safe."}},[182]={k="752",["end"]={d=776,t="You started by fetching water for Greatmother Hawkwind, a humble act that caught the eye of the Chief. He sent you to Baine Bloodhoof, who passed you to Zarlman Two-Moons. After brewing the Water of the Seers from well stones and ambercorn, you drank before the fire and followed a vision to Red Rocks. The Ancestral Spirits blessed you there, granting you entrance to Thunder Bluff. Standing before Cairne Bloodhoof, you proved your worth by tracking the mighty kodo Arra'chea across Mulgore and claiming its horn. Your hunt provided meat for the tribe, finally cementing your honored place among your people."},mid={d=767,t="You began with a simple act of care, seeking out Greatmother Hawkwind by the quiet well outside Camp Narache. Sparing her weary legs, you hauled her heavy water pitcher back to Chief Hawkwind. Impressed by your dedication to the tribe, the Chief entrusted you with his carved totem and sent you down the dusty road to Bloodhoof Village. There, Baine Bloodhoof recognized the mark of his friend and welcomed you to continue your trials. He sent you to the spiritual leader, Zarlman Two-Moons, who sensed your arrival before you even spoke. You have traveled far to prove your worth to the distant elders of Thunder Bluff, but what truths the holy land will reveal to your eyes remains an impenetrable mystery."}},[183]={k="6365",["end"]={d=6386,t="You brought Zargh's prime cuts of meat to Devrak at the Crossroads, then soared upon a wind rider to Orgrimmar. There, you delivered the gift to Innkeeper Gryshka. The fine steaks won her favor, and she entrusted you with a letter of gratitude. With the help of Doras, you rode the swift winds back to the Barrens and placed her reply into Zargh's hands. He was thrilled by her warm response. Your simple deliveries kindled an unexpected spark of romance in a harsh land. It proved that even a humble offering can forge a lasting connection."}},[184]={k="5726",["end"]={d=5730,t="You claimed a cultist's insignia from Skull Rock, proving your worth to Thrall. At his command, you carried that mark into the Cleft of Shadow to deceive Neeru Fireblade, posing as a loyal servant of the Burning Blade. Moving in secret, you descended into Ragefire Chasm and assassinated Bazzalan and Jergosh, crippling the cult's leadership beneath the city. Your deception was flawless. An unsuspecting Neeru confessed that the Shadow Council was shifting its dark work into the Barrens and Ashenvale. You have rooted out the immediate threat to Orgrimmar, arming the Warchief with vital intelligence against the rot spreading through his lands."},before={a=5728,t="You earned Thrall's trust when he could rely on no other. The Warchief suspected a treacherous rot within his own city, an infection he could not purge openly without causing it to spread. He sent you into the dark of Skull Rock to expose the Burning Blade, and you returned with a lieutenant's insignia. Armed with that token, you descended into the Cleft of Shadow to deceive the warlock who secretly leads this vile cult. Believing you were one of his own, he unknowingly revealed the names of his most valued allies. Now, the trap is set. Thrall has directed you into the fiery depths of Ragefire Chasm to sever the cult's power. You are to find the satyr Bazzalan and the warlock leader of the Searing Blade, and execute them. But you must strike without letting Neeru discover your true loyalties, preserving your identity as a dedicated member of his twisted brotherhood."}},[185]={k="1431",["end"]={d=1436,t="You listened to Craven Drok speak of the Warchief's careful diplomacy, then sought out Keldran in his hovel. He revealed a grim political reality: the Alliance was pushing deeper into Kalimdor, and any lingering demonic presence could be mistaken for a renewed pact between the Horde and the Burning Legion. Sent far to the west into Desolace, you found Takata Steelblade struggling against a rampant demon infestation. By purging the corruption, you did more than just indirectly aid the native centaur. You silenced damning rumors before they could begin, proving to a wary world that the Horde's dark history remains buried."}},[187]={k="5722",["end"]={d=5724,t="Rahauro sent you into the darkest tunnels of Orgrimmar to search Ragefire Chasm for Maur Grimtotem. Magatha believed her servant found something peculiar there before vanishing. Deep within the earth, you discovered his battered corpse, beaten to death by savage troggs. Yet even in his brutal end, Maur still tightly clutched a satchel in his arms, defending his discovery to his dying breath. You pried the Grimtotem Satchel from his lifeless grasp and carried it safely back to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff. Your work is done, ensuring whatever Maur unearthed is now firmly in the hands of the Grimtotem clan."},before={a=5722,t="Word reached you of a servant lost to the dark. Rahauro spoke of Maur Grimtotem, an emissary sent into the depths of Ragefire Chasm to parley with the brutish troggs that dwell beneath Orgrimmar. Maur had discovered something unusual in those shadowed caverns, a secret he intended to bring back to Magatha. But the earth swallowed him, and neither he nor his prize ever returned to the surface. You heard the grim tale, accepting the burden of uncovering the lost servant's fate. The trail leads downward, into the sweltering volcanic underworld. You must seek his remains, assuming the hostile tunnels have not completely consumed them. Whatever strange artifact or forbidden knowledge he uncovered must be reclaimed from the heat and ash. Now, you must descend into the darkest reaches of the city, brave the troggs, and pull Maur's corpse from the chasm along with any trace of his discovery."}},[189]={k="120",["end"]={d=146,t="You carried Magistrate Solomon's desperate pleas across the kingdom, seeking aid for the besieged town of Lakeshire. First you sought the Stormwind Army, but General Marcus Jonathan offered only vague promises of support. You then rode to Westfall, where Gryan Stoutmantle's militia fought their own lonely war. Finally, you braved the roads of Duskwood, but Lord Ello Ebonlocke refused to sacrifice his Night Watch. Every leader you spoke to revealed the same bitter truth: Stormwind had abandoned its people to fend for themselves. Solomon now understands that treachery has taken root in the capital, leaving the outer regions defenseless."}},[202]={k="421",["end"]={d=99,t="To prove yourself to Dalar Dawnweaver, you struck down the Moonrage Whitescalps stalking Silverpine Forest. Searching for the roots of Arugal's reckless sorcery, you tore a forgotten remedy from an abandoned farm and stripped enchanted shackles from the wandering beasts. You secured the Deep Elem Mine for the Forsaken, severing the head of Grimson the Pale. Lastly, you gathered twisted bindings from the cursed peasants of Pyrewood Village, who turn from men into savage worgen at nightfall. Through your relentless bloodshed, Dawnweaver finally possesses the knowledge to undo Arugal's magic, opening the path for the Dark Lady to conquer the forest."}},[203]={k="428",["end"]={d=425,t="You set out into northern Silverpine to search for two missing Deathstalkers. You found Rane and Quinn Yorick at a farm, where Quinn lay severely wounded after an attack by a ghoul. To save him, you hunted worgs for their discolored hearts and traveled to the Sepulcher, returning with a healing potion from Apothecary Renferrel. Once Quinn took the medicine, you turned your attention to the monster that maimed him. You cornered Ivar the Foul in a nearby barn and struck him down. With the beast slain and his head delivered as proof, the Deathstalkers were finally safe, their survival ensured."}},[204]={k="435",["end"]={d=1358,t="You led Deathstalker Erland safely past the ravenous wolves of Silverpine Forest to reach Rane Yorick. After carrying their urgent report on the Scourge to High Executor Hadrec, you were summoned by Apothecary Renferrel. He had discovered a baffling, deadly toxin within the wolves' hearts. You brought his samples to Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity, who quickly realized the dark potential of this discovery. She sent you across the sea, bearing the tainted flesh to Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads. Now, this strange Lordaeron poison rests in his hands, ready to advance the deadly knowledge of the Forsaken."}},[205]={k="437",["end"]={d=442,t="You destroyed the banshee Nightlash at the Dead Fields, then followed the Decrepit Ferry's trail of stolen corpses across Lordamere Lake to Fenris Isle. By delivering the rot hides' tainted blood to the Undercity, you unearthed the architect of this macabre harvest: Thule Ravenclaw, a treacherous mage allied with the Scourge. Armed with counter-magics, you stormed his island stronghold and severed his head. His destruction released a surge of arcane power felt miles away. The corpse trade has been halted, and you have struck a resounding blow against the Lich King's grasp on these plagued lands."},mid={d=443,t="You struck out against the rot hide gnolls at the Dead Fields, destroying the banshee Nightlash to break the Scourge's momentum. But the threat was deeper than a simple camp. Pressing east to the Decrepit Ferry, you found a ruined boat heaped with stolen corpses bound for Fenris Isle across Lordamere Lake. An engraved ring worn by a recently slain woman confirmed the grim truth: the dead were being dragged from the mass graves of Tirisfal. Seeking the architect of this dark harvest, you crossed to the island and extracted the foul ichor pumping through the gnolls' veins. Now, Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher studies this vile fluid, hoping to uncover a weakness and learn who truly commands the rot hides in the shadows."}},[206]={k="477",["end"]={d=480,t="You tracked the shipments of the Dalaran wizards to a camp north of Pyrewood Village, where you uncovered old maps and a magical pendant. Shadow Priest Allister sent the artifact to Dalar Dawnweaver for study. He revealed the truth: the Kirin Tor intended to channel power through the pendants to reactivate a dormant ley energy node within Ambermill. You fought through the town's defenders, stripping them of their artifacts to slow their ritual. Finally, you struck down the archmage guiding the spellwork and claimed his staff. The magic dissipated, silencing the ley node and striking a heavy blow against the human forces."}},[208]={k="6421",["end"]={d=6481,t="You journeyed deep into Boulderslide Ravine, investigating the frantic mining of Resonite crystals by the local kobolds. Bringing samples back to Mor'rogal revealed a dire threat: the kobolds had dug too deep and unearthed a slumbering Earthen named Goggeroc. These ancient beings were forged by the Titans to shape the world, and such raw power could not go unchecked. Armed with an enchanted crystal, you shattered Goggeroc's prison and struck down the weakened giant. Through your decisive victory, you eliminated a profound danger, ensuring this primordial wrath would not rise to threaten Stonetalon and all of Kalimdor."}},[211]={k="1077",["end"]={d=1084,t="Armed with Gaxim Rustfizzle's explosives, you infiltrated the Venture Co. lumber mill. Your sabotage provided the cover to steal their engineering plans and confidential letters, dealing a heavy blow to their deforesting efforts. Delivering these secrets to Kaela Shadowspear exposed the true horror of the goblins' retreat. They had set the Vale ablaze, awakening enraged spirits of flame and stone that you were forced to strike down. Even the noble treants were corrupted by the goblins' destructive weapons. By gathering the shrapnel lodged within the wounded ancients, you gave the Sentinels the means to understand the strange corruption plaguing the forest."}},[212]={k="1483",["end"]={d=1096,t="You found the disgruntled goblin Ziz Fizziks in Windshear Crag, furious that the Venture Company replaced him with a gnome named Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle. To secure his place in the Tinkers' Union, you stole blueprints for a massive woodcutting machine and delivered them to Sputtervalve in Ratchet. But corporate espionage was not enough for the trade princes. They demanded the gnome's death. Returning to the crag, you climbed high above the lake to confront Gerenzo, a twisted engineer with mechanical limbs grafted to his rotting flesh. Now the cyborg gnome lies dead, a brutal message delivered, and Ziz hopes his new masters will finally welcome him home."}},[220]={k="343",["end"]={d=346,t="You set out to fetch a book on metallurgy for Brother Kristoff, but retrieving The Stresses of Iron proved complicated. Stormwind's librarian sent you to Northshire Abbey, where you discovered Brother Paxton's copying work halted by a dried ink supply. Seeking rare Rethban ore to brew more, you traveled to Lakeshire only to find the supplier busy preparing for orc attacks. Descending into the gnoll-infested Rethban Caverns to mine the stone yourself, you delivered the raw ore to the abbey. Your efforts allowed the scribe to finish his copy, ensuring Brother Kristoff received his original tome so the wisdom within could be shared."}},[221]={k="3765",["end"]={d=1275,t="Argos Nightwhisper found you in the bustling streets of Stormwind, sending you across the sea to aid his brother in Auberdine. There, Gershala shared a grim fear: that the blood elves' meddling with demonic magic would twist them into monsters. To uncover the truth of their impending fate, he needed you to hunt the corrupted creatures haunting the coast of Ashenvale. You descended into Blackfathom Deeps, claiming the corrupted remains of naga and satyr alike. With the grim trophies delivered, Gershala now begins his vital study, searching for answers that might spare Azeroth from another monstrous threat."},before={a=1275,t="You heard the plea of Argos Nightwhisper amidst the bustling activity of Stormwind. Seeking an experienced druid for an epic journey, he sent you far across the world to the region of Darkshore. Arriving in the coastal town of Auberdine, you met with his brother, Gershala Nightwhisper. He shared his grave fears regarding the blood elves and their reckless meddling with demonic magic. Gershala worried they would soon suffer the same twisted, monstrous deformation that long ago befell the naga and the satyrs of Kalimdor. Hoping to uncover the dark path the elves are walking and prevent the birth of another vile race, he asked you to retrieve the brain stems of those corrupted beings for his studies. Now, you must embark on a long road to the shores of Ashenvale, where both satyr and naga await within the treacherous depths of Blackfathom Deeps."}},[222]={k="337",["end"]={d=542,t="You lifted a muddy, scratched history book from the dirt and returned it to the shelves of Stormwind. Trusting your dedication, the library sent you far north to salvage more. The old kingdom of Alterac lay in ruins after the great war, its vast collection of tomes left to the brutish ogres now squatting in the rubble. You traveled to Southshore, then braved the crumbling walls of Alterac itself. Tearing the stolen books from the beasts' grasp, you secured a worn leather text containing ancient troll lore. In a world scarred by conflict, you ensured that the wisdom of the past would survive."}},[265]={k="4495",["end"]={d=3522,t="Dirania Silvershine feared for her missing friend, and your search led you into the shadowed depths of the northern cave. There, you found Iverron succumbing to the virulent poison of Githyiss the Vile. Racing against his fading life, you gathered Hyacinth mushrooms, Moonpetal lilies, and Webwood ichor from the spiders that bit him. You dashed back through the darkness, delivering Dirania's volatile antidote before time ran out. The serum purged the venom from his veins. You spared a foolish explorer a wretched death, proving that even in these venomous shadows, swift action can snatch a life back from the brink."}},[266]={k="916",mid={d=921,t="You ventured into the shadowed depths of Shadowglen, seeking to understand the strange new beasts of the forest. Guided by Gilshalan Windwalker, you braved Shadowthread Cave, prying toxic venom and an unhatched egg from the giant webwood spiders. With these specimens bound for Darnassus to reveal the new world tree's influence, you ascended to the heights of Aldrassil. There, you answered the summons of Tenaron Stormgrip. He spoke of a changed people, of the victory at Mount Hyjal, and of ancient Nordrassil left a pale shadow of its former glory. At his behest, you drew sacred waters from the moonwell. Yet the full story of the battle's aftermath remains veiled, and the true destiny waiting for you within the greater expanse of Teldrassil is still a mystery."},["end"]={d=935,t="You began by harvesting venom and an unhatched egg from the giant webwood spiders, discovering the strange mutations caused by the new world tree. Drawn into the tragic history of your people, you journeyed between the moonwells of Teldrassil to gather their sacred waters. With each filled vessel, you learned the bitter truth of this land. Planted without the blessings of Nozdormu and Alexstrasza, the great tree is fundamentally flawed, driving the native beasts to madness. You have delivered the combined waters to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus. Now he must bear the weight of his arrogant creation, hoping these waters can cure its spreading corruption."}},[267]={k="997",["end"]={d=2499,t="You delivered rare earth to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth, where the timberlings had grown angry and erratic. Gathering their seeds, you sought answers from Rellian Greenspyre in Darnassus, who discovered a deep corruption had tainted the elementals. You purged the twisted creatures at Wellspring Lake, tearing away the mossy tumors that poisoned them. Yet the true source lay hidden back at Lake Al'Ameth. Deep within a southern cave, a gargantuan tumor had corrupted Oakenscowl, a noble leader among his kind. You struck down the mighty creature and secured the massive blight. Now Denalan can study the disease that threatens Teldrassil, hoping to save its natural order."}},[270]={k="488",["end"]={d=489,t="Lured by hidden promises, you became a willing servant to the satyr Zenn Foulhoof. You slaughtered the creatures of Teldrassil to supply his reagents, only to find yourself mocked as a gullible pawn. Your reckless bloodshed drew the ire of the Council of the Forest, who demanded you atone for defiling their woods. To earn back their trust, you gathered corrupted fel cones and presented them to the satyr as an innocent treat. He swallowed your tainted offering without a second thought. By answering trickery with trickery, you restored your honor and ensured the foul beast suffered for his deceit."}},[271]={k="4542",["end"]={d=5064,t="You delivered Brave Moonhorn's warning of worsening attacks to Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post. Discovering that a caravan had been massacred, you ventured north and struck down the centaur assailants in retribution. But a separate, shadowy threat loomed over the bluffs. Following reports of strange outsiders, you scaled the heights of Darkcloud Pinnacle to pilfer hidden missives from the Grimtotem Clan. The stolen documents you brought back exposed a sweeping conspiracy. With this chilling revelation now in the hands of its defenders, Freewind Post must brace itself against an impending danger."}},[272]={k="1149",["end"]={d=1394,t="You hurled yourself into the unknown to prove your spirit to Dorn Plainstalker, then waded through the Roguefeather Den to fell Grenka Bloodscreech. In the dust of Thousand Needles, you shattered the ancient elemental Rok'Alim. Yet flesh and bone are only half the measure of a champion. Seeking deeper truths, you braved the slayers of Dor'danil to claim the Legacy of the Aspects for Braug Dimspirit, and finally journeyed to Lordaeron City to satisfy the skeptical scholar Parqual Fintallas. Through brutal combat and quiet study, your body, mind, and spirit were relentlessly tested and found unbreakable. You stand now as a truly enlightened warrior."},mid={d=1154,t="You sought out Dorn Plainstalker to prove the strength of your spirit, body, and mind. Your journey began with a blind leap into the unknown, trusting faith alone to carry you through adversity. With your spirit steeled, you pushed your flesh to its limits. Deep in a harpy den, you provoked and slaughtered Grenka Bloodscreech, then hunted down Rok'Alim, an ancient elemental lingering in Thousand Needles. Having proven your endurance and physical might, you were sent north to find the shaman Braug Dimspirit. Dismissing your past battles as childish, he commanded you to brave the haunted depths of Dor'danil and recover a heavy tome guarded by dead druids. You have returned with the book in hand, but the true trial of your intellect remains. What ancient secrets will the shaman demand you recall?"}},[273]={k="4821",["end"]={d=5088,t="You sought an alien egg in the serpent dens of Thousand Needles, but its retrieval revealed a terrible truth. A legendary spirit of vengeance, Arikara, had awakened. To defeat her, you harvested rare agave from the Boiling Pool and delivered it to Magatha Grimtotem in Thunder Bluff. Armed with her enchanted powder, you ignited a sacred flame atop the Darkcloud Pinnacle, drawing the beast into battle. You struck the creature down, yet your victory leaves a lingering doubt. Motega Firemane praised your success, but the claim that Arikara was hunting Cairne Bloodhoof left him unsettled. The immediate threat is gone, but the mystery endures."}},[274]={k="1100",["end"]={d=1101,t="You discovered a battered journal upon a fallen dwarf and delivered it to Falfindel Waywarder. Its worn pages detailed the bitter ends of both Henrig Lonebrow and Heralath. Realizing that Charlga Razorflank was responsible, you gathered allies and plunged into the perilous depths of the Kraul. Deep within those thorns, you fought your way to the crone and struck her down, taking her medallion to prove the deed was done. Your victory ensures researchers can safely investigate what foul corruption blights the resting grounds of Agamaggan, even as they begin to fear that deeper treachery lies behind the rot."},before={a=1101,t="You stumbled upon the weathered journal of Henrig Lonebrow, plucked from the cold grip of the deceased dwarf in the wilderness. Seeking guidance, you carried its bleak pages to Falfindel Waywarder. As he studied the grim accounts, Falfindel read of the bitter ends met by the brave Lonebrow and poor Heralath. He knew their valiant sacrifices simply could not be allowed to fade into nothing. A sinister hand had guided their untimely doom: the wicked crone known as Charlga Razorflank. With the threat mounting rapidly and no time left to send word to distant Darnassus for aid, the heavy weight of vengeance fell directly to you. Now, you must assemble a loyal party and undertake a perilous infiltration into the dark, tangled depths of the Kraul. Your only path forward is to slay the crone where she dwells, and to claim Razorflank's Medallion as undeniable proof of her demise."}},[281]={k="6361",["end"]={d=6364,t="You carried a bundle of hides from the Crossroads to Thunder Bluff, soaring high above the Barrens on the back of a wind rider. At your destination, Ahanu worked those raw pelts into fine leather goods. Taking to the skies once more, you returned the finished wares to Jahan Hawkwing. Your journey was a simple errand, yet it solidified a vital trade link between the growing settlements. By bringing these durable leathers back to the Crossroads, you equipped the countless travelers flocking to the outpost, giving them the means to survive in an unforgiving territory."}},[282]={k="1061",["end"]={d=1086,t="The spirits of the Stonetalon Mountains cried out as the Venture Company tore down the forests. You answered their pain with violence, but simple bloodshed was not enough. In Thunder Bluff, Magatha Grimtotem guided you toward the dark arts of the Forsaken. Traveling to distant Tarren Mill, you took stolen innocent blood from Syndicate mages so Apothecary Lydon could brew a devastating toxin. Armed with Zamah's refined poison, you infiltrated the goblin camps and planted the payload at their hidden flying machine airport. The insidious brew now spreads toward their headquarters, crippling the plunderers and securing a ruthless victory for the land."},mid={d=1064,t="You heard the cries of the anguished land and journeyed to the Stonetalon Mountains, finding the shaman Seereth Stonebreak. She spoke of the Venture Company goblins tearing down the forests, their relentless logging driving the local spirits mad with pain and rage. Heeding her call, you marched into the Windshear Crag and slaughtered the timber workers in a bloody display of the Horde's resolve. Yet, calming the enraged spirits demanded wisdom beyond brute force. Seereth sent you to the heights of Thunder Bluff to consult the elder, Magatha Grimtotem. Believing the land must be cleansed of its disease first, Magatha guided you to Apothecary Zamah in the shadowy Pools of Vision, leaving it uncertain what unnatural remedies the Forsaken emissary might unleash to mend the broken earth."}},[283]={k="1195",["end"]={d=1197,t="You traveled far into Ashenvale Forest, securing a small phial from the dryads and filling it from a sacred moonwell. Carrying this precious fluid south to the Freewind Post in the Thousand Needles, you learned its magic could pierce the fiery defenses of a fiercely protected treasure. Striking into Splithoof Hold, you battled the savage Galak centaur and used the gathered water to briefly smother the undying fires, seizing a revered relic. Delivering the ancient hoof to Rau Cliffrunner revealed a pulsing power within it, an unknown force that will finally unravel the hidden origins of their entire race."}},[285]={k="363",["end"]={d=383,t="You woke in the crypt of Deathknell, freed from the Lich King's iron will. Under the guidance of Undertaker Mordo and Shadow Priest Sarvis, you struck down the mindless undead haunting your new home and gathered supplies to aid your survival. After clearing out a spider-infested gold mine, you turned your sights on the fanatical Scarlet Crusade. Intercepting their messenger, you claimed a vital map and delivered it to Executor Zygand in Brill. With the locations of the crusade's field commanders now in Forsaken hands, your people are primed to sever the leadership of those zealous foes."}},[286]={k="367",["end"]={d=492,t="You answered the call of Lady Sylvanas to help the Royal Apothecary Society forge a disease deadly enough to break Arthas and his Scourge. In Brill, you aided Apothecary Johaan, harvesting darkhound blood, murloc scales, and the venom of vicious night web spiders to perfect the deadly brew. Once the boiling concoction was complete, it fell to you to test it. Descending into the cellar of the Gallows End Tavern, you offered the drink to a captured dwarven mountaineer. He drank deeply to quench his thirst, his impending doom a grim taste of the terrifying future the Dark Lady plans for all of Azeroth."}},[288]={k="358",["end"]={d=411,t="You proved your worth to Magistrate Sevren by slaughtering the Rot Hide gnolls that gathered corpses for the Scourge. Recognizing your strength, he sent you to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity. At Bethor's behest, you stole a spellbook from an isolated lich upon Brightwater Lake, revealing him to be the former Kirin Tor mage, Gunther Arcanus. After you returned the enchanted book and destroyed the Scourge agent Lillith Nefara, Gunther finally realized he was not the only undead freed from the Lich King's grasp. He entrusted you with a Nether Gem, ending his isolation and securing his formidable necromantic knowledge for the Forsaken."}},[289]={k="427",["end"]={d=372,t="Armed with intercepted documents, you systematically dismantled the Scarlet Crusade across Tirisfal Glades. Executor Zygand directed your wrath against their footholds. You began by culling the warriors occupying the tower beyond the Solliden Farmstead. Next, you hunted their officers. You struck a ruined tower to assassinate Captain Perrine and his zealots. You then moved against Captain Vachon near the Balnir Farmstead. Finally, you marched past Faol's Rest to strike down the ruthless Captain Melrache. By shattering their leadership, you halted the crusade's advance. Your bloodshed pleased the Dark Lady and brought the Forsaken one step closer to their ultimate revenge against Arthas."}},[292]={k="6321",["end"]={d=6324,t="You took a requisition order from Deathguard Podrig at the Sepulcher, flying through the gloom to the Undercity. There, you found the weapons dealer Gordon Wendham and handed him the request. He packed a heavy crate of armaments, which you brought back across the skies to the remote outpost in Silverpine. Now, the Deathguards stand ready with fresh steel to fend off the Scourge lurking in the woods. By securing these vital supplies, you made certain that the grim servants of the Dark Lady will not be caught unprepared when the shadows inevitably close in."}},[295]={k="6981A",["end"]={d=3370,t="You found a brilliant, unsettling green crystal swirling with smoky depths and brought it to Ratchet, seeking answers. Falla Sagewind examined the shard, recognizing it as the pure essence of the Emerald Dream, but she recoiled at the dark visions within. She urged you to take the nightmare-tainted stone to Darnassus. There, you entrusted it to Mathrengyl Bearwalker. When he peered into the glass, the grim truth shook him. He locked the danger away, warning that the realm of nature slumbers in unseen peril. You have delivered a dark secret to the Cenarion druids, who alone must face whatever corruption now stirs beneath the dream."},before={a=6981,t="You uncovered a shard of brilliant green crystal, completely solid to the touch. Yet, just beneath its smooth surface, shadows that looked exactly like thick smoke swirled and shifted continuously. Your eyes were drawn deep into the heart of the stone, mesmerized by the silent, unnatural movement trapped inside. A strange fascination took hold of your mind, making it nearly impossible to look away from the emerald depths. However, even as you stared, a creeping sense of dread washed over you. The longer you held the heavy crystal, the more certain you became that there was something deeply and fundamentally disturbing about its very nature. The origin of the corrupt relic remained a complete mystery, but ignoring its existence was simply not an option. Needing answers, you turned your attention toward the arid shores to the east. You set out to see if anyone in Ratchet can tell you more about this strange shard."}},[296]={k="6981H",["end"]={d=3369,t="You found a vibrant green crystal with smoke swirling beneath its solid shell. Disturbed by its unnatural aura, you carried the unsettling stone to Falla Sagewind in Ratchet. She recognized the artifact as a pure piece of the Emerald Dream, yet saw only a horrifying nightmare trapped inside. Unwilling to keep it, she sent you far away to Thunder Bluff. There, you gave the burden to Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise. He warned you to forget the matter, but his unease proved the worst. You surrendered the shard, but a grim truth remains: corruption infects the Emerald Dream."},before={a=6981,t="You discovered a brilliant green shard, a stone unlike any you had ever seen. Though its crystalline surface felt completely solid and unyielding in your hands, a restless energy seemed trapped within. When you looked closely, it was as if thick, dark smoke swirled continually just beneath the surface, shifting and churning with a life of its own. You found yourself utterly captivated, unable to pull your gaze away from the hypnotic depths of the crystal. Yet, beneath that strange fascination, a profound sense of unease washed over you. A creeping dread whispered in your mind, warning you that there was something fundamentally and deeply disturbing about the object you now carried. It was not a natural thing, and the heavy burden of its dark presence weighed upon you. Seeking answers to ease your troubled thoughts, you turn your steps toward the coast. Now, you set out for Ratchet, seeking anyone who might tell you more about this strange shard."}},[298]={k="6181",["end"]={d=6285,t="You carried a desperate plea from the defenders of Sentinel Hill to the bustling streets of Stormwind. Borne upon a winged gryphon, you soared high above the forests to secure armor for an outpost the kingdom had all but forgotten. In the city's heart, you gathered the heavy crates of steel and leather, bringing them safely back through the clouds. The embattled soldiers received the protection they desperately needed to hold the line. Through this vital trade, you forged a lasting link across the open skies, proving that help was never more than a flight away."}},[300]={k="92742",["end"]={d=92819,t="You sought the source of the poison choking the farmlands of Westfall, drawing water from tainted wells and searching the shoreline. When the local mines yielded no answers, a trail of suspicious supplies led you deep into the abandoned Deadmines. You journeyed to Stormwind, gathering dynamite and a remote detonator from the shadows of SI:7, before returning to plant your bomb inside a sprawling, hidden forge. The blast brought the machinery crashing down, halting the flow of toxins. Yet the devastation was no mere bandit scheme. It was driven by Stormwind's endless hunger for war, sacrificing the very earth and citizens the kingdom was meant to defend."},mid={d=92748,t="You drew water from the wells at the Jansen Stead and the Molsen Farm, seeking the source of the poison plaguing Westfall. You scoured the shoreline for murloc gills, proving the corruption had not yet reached the sea. When the well samples revealed toxic metals, you struck down the Defias laborers in the Jangolode Mine and the Gold Coast Quarry. Yet the poison flowed from elsewhere. You searched the abandoned town of Moonbrook, uncovering heavy industrial supplies that pointed to a massive, hidden operation. You traveled to the Dwarven District of Stormwind, seeking an engineer whose explosives might shatter whatever machinery chokes the land. But what sprawling industry churns in the black depths of the Deadmines, and whose hands guide its toxic work, remains unknown."}},[301]={k="136",["end"]={d=140,t="A map left by the late Captain Sanders set you on a long hunt across Westfall. You unearthed his sandy footlocker by a rusted anchor on the western coast, snatching a clue from a scurrying crab. Trekking eastward up the bluffs to a ruined chimney, you uncovered the next piece inside a broken barrel. Following it north to a lone windmill, you extracted a whiskey-soaked note from an empty jug. Guided to the shore, you swam west to an island and forced open his locked chest. Captain Sanders may rest in a watery grave, but you claimed the fortune he left behind."}},[310]={k="473",["end"]={d=474,t="You answered Valstag Ironjaw's summons and stood before Captain Stoutfist as the Dragonmaw clan gathered strength. Decimated in the Second War, these orcs rallied under Chieftain Nek'rosh in a bitter bid for revenge. You waded into their camp to claim their war banners, then uncovered a far more immediate threat: a planned siege on Menethil Harbor. Striking with fire, you reduced their catapults to smoldering ash. In the ensuing chaos, you claimed Nek'rosh's head. By destroying both the leader and his siege engines, you broke the Dragonmaw's resurgence and secured the safety of the harbor, winning the favor of Ironforge."}},[311]={k="288",["end"]={d=293,t="You met the sole survivor of the Third Fleet drowning his memories. First Mate Fitzsimmons spoke of the dragonfire that doomed his ships and a dark treasure that chained his fallen crew. Wading into the wreckage, you put his restless shipmates to the sword and struck down Captain Halyndor. Within the sunken ruins, you recovered the relic responsible for their torment: an Eye of Paleth. When Glorin Steelbrow failed to purge its malice, you carried the tainted orb to Stormwind. There, Archbishop Benedictus cleansed the artifact of its deep sorrow, lifting the curse and finally allowing the dead sailors of Kul Tiras to find peace."}},[312]={k="303",["end"]={d=378,t="When the Dark Iron dwarves ravaged the Thandol Span and seized Dun Modr, you did not wait for the reserves. You pushed the front lines back, spilling blood to break their encampment and buy King Magni's loyal soldiers a fighting chance. But justice demanded more than holding the territory. Learning that Kam Deepfury orchestrated the assault that claimed the life of Longbraid's brother, you tracked the conspirator to his cell in the Stormwind Stockade. By taking his head, you bypassed his political shielding to deliver a swift execution. His death grants solace to the mourning families, proving that no coward can hide from vengeance."},before={a=378,t="You stood amidst the wreckage of Dun Modr, a grim testament to the devastation on the home front. While the armies of the Alliance fought in distant lands, the Dark Iron Dwarves struck with ruthless precision, crippling the Thandol Span. Answering the call of Motley Garmason, you waded into the fray. You struck down their tunnelers and saboteurs, applying enough pressure to halt their advance while hoping the reserves might finally arrive. Your valor proved your unwavering loyalty to King Magni. Yet, a deeper betrayal drove the conflict. Garmason revealed that intelligence gathered by Roggo pointed to a conspirator behind the destruction of the Thandol Span, the very act that cost Longbraid his kin. That architect of ruin, Kam Deepfury, is currently protected by political maneuvering, held within the confines of the Stormwind Stockade. You now march to the capital, tasked to breach those prison walls and return with his head."}},[314]={k="631",["end"]={d=634,t="You found poor Ebenezer Rustlocke dead at the Thandol Span, clutching orders that laid bare a Dark Iron plot. Kam Deepfury meant to shatter the last crossing and cut off the north from Khaz Modan. You destroyed the hidden stockpile of explosives before it could be triggered, preserving the vital route. Yet when you rode into the Arathi Highlands to beg Captain Nials for reinforcements, you found only more disaster. With Stromgarde fallen, the soldiers at Refuge Pointe were trapped in their own desperate struggle. The bridge remains whole, but Longbraid and his dwarves must hold Dun Modr on their own."}},[316]={k="92460A",["end"]={d=92472,t="You stepped into Thendal Village to come of age among the shen'dorei. Bearing an ancestral relic from Rorian the Dayseeker, you worked to restore the grove's delicate balance. You culled wild vuldren and quelled restless wind sprites driven to violence by the Al'Aketh cult. After you exposed these zealots, Elder Aetheen of the Gales tested your resolve against the vicious ursera matriarch, Urs'anah. Triumphant, you left the safety of the grove and traveled south to Shen'dar Village. Standing before Constable Aonda, you proved yourself more than a fledgling. You are a defender, ready to face the rising storm of the Al'Aketh."},mid={d=92465,t="You arrived in Thendal Village to mark your coming of age among the shen'dorei. Beneath the greatfather tree, Rorian the Dayseeker bestowed upon you an ancestral relic, a token of your people's resilience. Your first task was a simple one, thinning the local vuldren to preserve the grove's delicate balance, yet their restless nature hinted at deeper magical disturbances. Guided to the ancient standing stones, you met Yala Windwatcher, who discovered the true source of the unrest: the insidious Al'Aketh cult. Forced to shed the blood of your own kin, you dispersed the corrupted wind sprites and struck down the zealots. You have driven back the cultists for now, but what drove them to agitate the winds in the first place remains a mystery."}},[317]={k="92460H",["end"]={d=92472,t="You came of age in Thendal Village, receiving your relic from Rorian the Dayseeker. You culled the restless vuldren and fought through the winds to strike down the Al'Aketh cultists hiding in the grove. After bringing word of this threat to the elders, you proved your strength to Aetheen of the Gales by slaying the savage matriarch Urs'anah. Your trials completed, you left the safety of the village and journeyed south. You presented yourself to Constable Aonda in Shen'dar Village, offering your newly proven might to stand against the growing darkness of the cult."},mid={d=92465,t="You arrived at Thendal Village, eager to prove yourself, and received a sacred relic from Rorian the Dayseeker at the greatfather tree. It bound you to the history of the shen'dorei and the winds of Zephras. But peace in Thendal Grove was fragile. You soon had to cull the local vuldren, docile creatures driven to unpredictable behavior by imbalanced magic. When simple wind sprites near the standing stones grew agitated, Rorian sent you to Yala Windwatcher. She discovered that the Al'Aketh cult had infiltrated the island, inciting the very air to violence. You struck down your corrupted kin and dispersed the roiling winds to protect your home. You quelled the immediate chaos, but the true motives driving the cult's dark work within the grove still remain an unsettling mystery."}},[10]={k="691",["end"]={d=697,t="You plunged into the untamed Arathi Highlands to aid Kryten and Skuerto, claiming vital reagents from Witherbark trolls and wresting a stolen wand from the ogre Kor'gresh. The true prize lay heavily guarded within the shattered walls of Stromgarde. Seizing a shamanic gem, you awakened the dormant defenses of the Tower of Arathor, parting a sea of Boulderfist ogres just enough to recover Trelane's most prized artifacts. You returned those ancient relics to Archmage Malin in Stormwind. Through your bloodshed in the highlands, a master's legacy was pulled back from the brink of ruin, and the mages' dangerous mission was finally brought to a close."}},[15]={k="665",["end"]={d=667,t="You protected Professor Phizzlethorpe from an ambush to power gnomish goggles, letting you pluck calcified elven gems from the sea floor. After delivering the sunken treasure to Captain Shakes O'Breen and carrying a sample south to Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay, you returned to the Arathi coast with secret orders. But the sea had its own plans. Daggerspine naga surged from the waves, intent on slaughtering the stranded pirates. Manning the ship's cannon, you drove the ruthless attackers back into the deep. O'Breen and his crew will sail home on the rising tide, owing their lives to you."}},[72]={k="1361",["end"]={d=1366,t="You answered Regthar Deathgate's call in the Barrens and marched into the brutal wastes of Desolace. There, Felgur Twocuts warned of a terrifying possibility: the warring centaur clans uniting against the Horde. To prevent this, you struck fast, assassinating Khan Dez'hepah to throw the Kolkar into chaos. But you did not stop at their leader. You swept across the dry plains, reaping a grisly harvest of ears from any centaur you found to bleed their numbers. You broke their resolve. Now, the surviving clans whisper your name in terror, knowing that the banner of the Horde casts a long, deadly shadow over their ancestral plains."}},[87]={k="317",["end"]={d=320,t="You scoured the frozen fields to outfit Pilot Bellowfiz for a grueling siege mission. After hauling meat and thick furs back to Steelgrill's Depot, his tank was nearly provisioned. But to brave the biting cold, the pilot needed a potent fuel—one that could warm his bones and power his steam engine alike. You traveled to Brewnall Village, culling the encroaching beasts of the snow so Rejold Barleybrew could brew in peace. With a heavy cask of his famous Evershine finally delivered into the pilot's eager hands, Jetsteam was prepared to face whatever danger the Siege Brigade pointed it toward."}},[122]={k="106",["end"]={d=114,t="You walked into the bitter feud between two farming families and chose to champion young love over old grudges. Carrying desperate letters across the fields, you sought the wisdom of an elder and the craft of an alchemist. You braved the murlocs of Crystal Lake to gather their strange kelp, returning to Goldshire to secure a potion of invisibility. With the brew safely in Maybell's hands, the lovers can finally steal a few precious moments together in the shadows. Though the bitter rivalry between their households remains unbroken, you proved that even in fractured lands, devotion can still find a way to bloom."}},[160]={k="533",["end"]={d=508,t="You scoured the Syndicate camps to find the captive expedition leader, Gol'dir, suffering under the cruel yoke of his human jailers. Hearing of Aliden Perenolde's twisted ambition to enslave the orcs just as his mentor Blackmoore once did, you brought swift justice to his manor by the lake. With the so-called lord dead, you spared his terrified mistress, Elysa, claiming the simple pendant she wore. Though it appears to be nothing more than a humble trinket, you have secured the prize the Warchief so deeply desired, settling a bitter grudge from the past."}},[161]={k="495",["end"]={d=521,t="You crushed an uprising born of a shiny trinket. Carving a bloody path through the snows of Alterac, you slaughtered the Crushridge ogres and severed the heads of Mug'Thol's lieutenants. Finally, you executed the rebellious leader himself, stripping the Crown of Will from his corpse before returning it to the shadows of the Undercity. Lady Sylvanas has her prize, and the artifact that broke her mental hold is secured. The butchered ogres now serve as a brutal, silent monument: none defy the Dark Lady and live."}},[196]={k="92401",["end"]={d=92401,t="You ventured into the blighted Ruins of Lordaeron, seeking Edward Heartweaver on behalf of his desperate wife. He had gone chasing ghosts, burdened by the guilt of a son lost to Arthas's wrath. In that fallen city, you uncovered the grim truth of his fate and brought it back to a grieving widow. The news brought her sorrow, but also a final, bitter closure. Though her gratitude was heavy with loss, your grim deed spared her from a lifetime of agonizing wonder."}},[229]={k="581",["end"]={d=592,t="You scoured Stranglethorn to find a lost Darkspear son. A grim harvest of Bloodscalp heads led to a dark bargain with severed spirits. To loosen their tongues, you broke the Skullsplitter chief. They revealed young Yenniku was enslaved by the outcast Zanzil. Striking down the ogre mage Mai'Zoth, you claimed the Mind's Eye. With that artifact forged into a Soul Gem, you broke Zanzil's hold and trapped the boy's freed spirit within. By delivering Yenniku to Nimboya, you rescued the chieftain's blood from eternal darkness. For this victory, your legend will be carved into Darkspear stone forever."},mid={d=586,t="Nimboya sent you into the dense jungles of Stranglethorn to uncover the fate of Yenniku, the lost son of a Darkspear chief. Fearing the boy fell to the savage Bloodscalp tribe, you carved a bloody path through their headhunters, gathering their gruesome trophies just to ensure the young troll's face was not among them. When the grim harvest yielded no answers, you severed the heads of the Bloodscalp leaders themselves, Gan'zulah and Nezzliok the Dire. Plunging their remains into a boiling cauldron, you bound the chieftain's spirit, only to be sent on a vengeful errand against the rival Skullsplitters. You shattered Ana'thek the Cruel to appease the furious ghost. Yet, despite the slaughter and dark rituals, the dead have not spoken the truth you seek. Yenniku's ultimate fate remains unknown."}},[232]={k="605",["end"]={d=600,t="In the sweltering depths of Stranglethorn, the goblin Crank Fizzlebub saw a chance for profit. At his behest, you hunted the hardened basilisks south of Zul'Kunda, harvesting the rare Singing Crystals from their hides. But beasts were not the only rivals for this glittering prize. The ruthless Venture Company tore at the hills near the Crystalvein Mine. You struck at their camps, prying the gems from their hands to deliver to an eager goblin. By your blade, the Venture Company's greedy grip on the jungle slipped just a fraction, all so a rival merchant could line his pockets."}},[238]={k="570",["end"]={d=573,t="You scoured the perilous jungles of Stranglethorn Vale to serve Far Seer Mok'thardin. First, you harvested the razor-sharp claws of the Shadowmaw Panthers and a pristine tigress fang. Next, you claimed vibrant feathers from the vicious Jungle Stalkers and the flawless sinew of an Elder Mistvale Gorilla. Finally, you fought through a ruthless expedition of naga to draw water from an ancient, contested Holy Spring. Woven together by the Far Seer's shamanic rituals, these wild reagents became a powerful enchanted choker. You wear it now as a symbol of your triumph, carrying the raw, untamed magic of the jungle in service to the Warchief and the Horde."}},[239]={k="595",["end"]={d=608,t="You started as a simple scout for First Mate Crazz, seeking the source of rumors along the Savage Coast. Finding a map detailing a Bloodsail invasion of Booty Bay thrust you into a deadly shadow war. You infiltrated their camp on the Wild Shore, stealing their charts and uncovering Firallon's grand design. Armed with that knowledge, you struck the true blow. You traveled down to the cape and assassinated the Bloodsail leadership before their ships could ever raise anchor. The Blackwater Raiders now celebrate their undisputed rule over Booty Bay, and an entire pirate fleet lies broken, headless, and adrift by your hand alone."}},[243]={k="624",["end"]={d=626,t="You followed the trail of a dead pirate's rhyming riddle across two continents, chasing a promise of hidden wealth. From a damp scroll beneath a bridge in the dismal Swamp of Sorrows, to a musty parchment hidden within a dangerous Dustwallow Marsh cave, you pieced together Cortello's final game. The chase ended far to the north, plunging into the rushing waters beneath the great falls of the Hinterlands. There, resting in the shadowed depths, you finally broke open the sunken chest. The long hunt is over, and the legendary treasure now belongs to you."}},[280]={k="1111",["end"]={d=1122,t="You crossed continents to line Kravel Koalbeard's pockets. From skimming gnome parts in Ratchet to trading Swamp of Sorrows dream dust for blackmail on a racer, you became an instrument of pure greed. But it was Crank Fizzlebub’s tainted brew, laced with Zanzil's poison, that secured the grand prize. By slipping the Fool's Stout to a racing pit boss, you rigged the odds and shattered an engine. Now, the bets are cashed, and the gold flows freely. The scheme is complete. You proved exactly how much ruin can be wrought for a simple cut of the profits."},mid={d=1116,t="You started as a simple courier for Kravel Koalbeard, fetching delayed shipments from Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet. But Kravel proved true to his opportunistic nature. After pocketing a choice piece of machinery from the delivery intended for Fizzle Brassbolts, his schemes shifted from petty theft to blackmail. He set his sights on Nazz Steamboil, a goblin racer in the Shimmering Flats hiding behind a false name. Tracking down this secret sent you far to the south, seeking Krazek in the bustling port of Booty Bay. The rumormonger demanded a steep price for his whispers, forcing you into the murky Swamp of Sorrows to harvest dream dust from dragon whelps. You delivered the coveted snuff into Krazek's hands, yet the dark truth behind the racer's discarded identity remains locked away in the rumormonger's greedy mind."}},[2]={k="511",["end"]={d=537,t="You pulled an encrypted letter from a Syndicate table in Alterac, unaware of the dark ties it concealed. When Loremaster Dibbs could not crack the cipher, you journeyed to Ironforge, where Prospector Stormpike laid bare its secrets. The translated text brought to Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore exposed a sinister alliance with a faction known as the Argus Wake. Following his orders, you marched into the Uplands, striking down the shadow mages and executing their master, Nagaz. Yet, this bloody work offers little comfort. Nagaz was merely a servant, and the shadowy grip of the Argus Wake may already threaten the entire world."}},[5]={k="522",["end"]={d=523,t="You uncovered a sealed contract marking Magistrate Maleb for death, a grim revelation you delivered to Southshore. The red wax bore the mark of the Syndicate, pointing to the cruel Baron Vardus of fallen Alterac. Tracking the treacherous noble through the ruined remnants of Strahnbrad, you met his brutality with your own steel. With Vardus dead, you severed the head of this lingering plot. The magistrate rests easier today, and the treacherous nobles of a ruined kingdom have learned they cannot strike from the shadows without facing justice."}},[13]={k="642A",["end"]={d=656,t="You heard the pleas of a trapped earth princess and broke the stones binding her beneath the Arathi Highlands. But Myzrael was no victim. She was a dark entity revered by the Twilight's Hammer, rightfully chained by the giants. To undo your mistake, you found the madman Theldurin the Lost in the Badlands and rebuilt the scroll to summon her. At the Shards of Myzrael, you dragged the deceiver to the surface, struck her down, and bound her with eldritch shackles. Her wail echoes from the deep, the crystal now pulsing with open malice. You corrected your error, but the earth still trembles."}},[14]={k="642H",["end"]={d=656,t="You answered the pleas of a trapped earth princess, freeing Myzrael from the ancient stones forged by giants. Her gratitude was a lie. You unwittingly unleashed a dark terror allied with the maddened Twilight's Hammer. Seeking to right your terrible wrong, you chased the rambling Theldurin the Lost into the Badlands, piecing together a torn scroll to force her hand. At the crystalline shards where she first deceived you, you dragged Myzrael to the surface and struck her down. Her eldritch shackles bind her once more deep beneath the Arathi Highlands. The earth groans with her fury, but the surface remains safe."}},[30]={k="720",["end"]={d=721,t="A desperate plea scribbled on a crumpled map sent you rushing to Prospector Ryedol. Fearing his friend Hammertoe had been dragged into Uldaman by the ruthless Shadowforge clan, Ryedol urged you to mount a rescue. The Dark Irons sought the captive dwarf's knowledge of titan excavations to forge terrible new golems, a threat Ironforge could not ignore. You descended into the ancient ruins and fought your way to the prisoner. You found Hammertoe battered, coughing, and barely clinging to life, but immensely relieved. You reached him before his mind could be broken, keeping the secrets of the titans safe from the enemy."}},[31]={k="707",["end"]={d=704,t="You traveled deep into the harsh sands of the Badlands, searching for a missing prospector. Instead of a living dwarf, you found only shattered bones and a bloody, dying message scrawled in the dirt. Honoring his grim end, you pushed into the Uldaman excavation and recovered the ancient urns he died trying to unearth. Now, those dusty relics rest safely in scholarly hands. Though Agmond met a brutal fate, his final discovery has provided a vital clue to understanding the savage troggs and the dark history buried beneath the stone."}},[32]={k="710",["end"]={d=778,t="In the scorched wastes of the Badlands, you broke the stone denizens of the earth to serve Lotwil Veriatus's dangerous ambition. From chipping away mere shards to claiming the heavy binding bracers of towering rock giants, you fed his volatile blend of arcane engineering. When Lucien Tosselwrench handed over the final cog and fled for cover, his terror was entirely justified. The arrogant mage's grand shackles failed spectacularly, unleashing a raging monstrosity instead of an obedient servant. You stood firm, breaking the destructive force before it could wreak havoc. Lotwil's groundbreaking history became just another foolish disaster, leaving you to clean up the pieces."}},[33]={k="718",["end"]={d=717,t="You began by helping Sigrun Ironhew recover abandoned supplies from scavenging ogres. Your reliability caught the eye of Garek, an agent of the Kirin Tor, who sent you to retrieve the stolen Sign of the Earth. You learned this artifact bound Blacklash and Hematus, two of Deathwing's ruthless lieutenants. Realizing their prison in Lethlor Ravine was no longer secure, you took drastic measures. You shattered the ancient seal, drew the black drakes out, and permanently ended their lives. Thanks to your bloody work, the skies are safe from their ancient wrath, and the Kirin Tor can finally rest easy."}},[34]={k="709A",["end"]={d=737,t="You plunged into the depths of Uldaman and brought back the Tablet of Ryun'eh, yet it was not enough to calm Theldurin's terrors. Bearing a dark sigil, you infiltrated a secret brotherhood in Ironforge, trading relics of forbidden power to Gerrig Bonegrip in exchange for Yagyin's Digest. Now, that cursed book rests in Theldurin's trembling hands. You secured the knowledge he begged for, a fragile weapon against ancient beings stirring beneath the earth. Whether this victory will actually spare the world from becoming worm food, or simply delay an inevitable doom, remains unseen."}},[35]={k="709H",["end"]={d=737,t="You braved the ancient depths of Uldaman, dragging the Tablet of Ryun'eh from a forgotten chest. But fragments of stone were not enough for the terrified dwarf. Carrying his false sigil into the Undercity, you traded relics of power to Keeper Bel'dugur for a dark, secret tome. Now, Theldurin clutches Yagyin's Digest in trembling hands, seeking salvation in its forbidden pages. You have given him a glimmer of hope against an unnamed doom sleeping beneath the earth. Whether this buried truth will truly save the world from ruin, or merely hasten its end, only time will tell."}},[36]={k="723",["end"]={d=762,t="You carried a dying dwarf's final plea from the dust of the Badlands to the high halls of Ironforge. Hammertoe Grez sacrificed everything to keep the lost artifacts of Uldaman out of Shadowforge hands. Through Prospector Ryedol and Historian Karnik, his amulet revealed a grave threat, securing Advisor Belgrum's swift blessing to strike back. In the depths of Angor Fortress, you struck down Ambassador Infernus, a fiery envoy of Ragnaros himself. With his defeat, the Shadowforge operations are crippled. Ironforge now prepares to reclaim their excavation site, their people safeguarded by the burden you bore for a fallen explorer."}},[73]={k="1382",["end"]={d=1380,t="You cast your lot with the Gelkis, shedding the blood of their rivals to prove your worth. You starved the Magram and humiliated the Kolkar, even traveling to the distant Swamp of Sorrows to claim a crystal of alien magic for Uthek the Wise. Empowered by your gifts, you severed the head of Khan Jehn. Finally, high in the Valley of Spears, you sounded a stolen horn to draw out Khan Hratha of the Maraudine. With his death, their clan is broken. The Gelkis now stand poised to rule the dusty plains of Desolace, and the spirits of the earth will echo your name forever."}},[74]={k="1385",["end"]={d=1381,t="You sought to control the warring centaur tribes of Desolace by elevating the Magram clan. You proved your ruthless strength to Warug, slaughtering the rival Kolkar and shattering the sacred crystals of the Gelkis. After fetching a strange mechanical toy to amuse the brute, you moved against the enemy leaders. You severed the head of Khan Shaka, then summoned and slew the Maraudine chieftain, Khan Hratha, claiming his key. The Magram now stand as the undisputed masters of the wasteland. You secured safety for the strongholds, earning a grim promise that you alone will be spared when the centaur hooves trample all others."}},[75]={k="1367",["end"]={d=1381,t="You threw your lot in with the Magram, cementing a brutal alliance in Gelkis blood. You shattered the tears of Theradras to break their rivals' faith, appeased the hulking Warug with a mechanical trinket, and brought him the severed head of Khan Shaka. Finally, you marched into the Valley of Spears, sounded a stolen horn, and slaughtered Khan Hratha of the Maraudine. With their greatest enemies crushed, the Magram now dominate the desolate wastes. You handed them the reins to this barren land, securing a rare promise that when their stampede begins, you alone will be spared."}},[76]={k="1368",["end"]={d=1380,t="To break the endless centaur wars of Desolace, you allied with the Gelkis. You starved their Magram rivals, then journeyed to a distant swamp to claim a strange red crystal from the lost one Ongeku for the shaman Uthek the Wise. With her magic empowered, you severed the head of the Magram by slaying Khan Jehn. Your bloody campaign culminated in the Valley of Spears, where you sounded a stolen horn to lure out the Maraudine leader, Khan Hratha. With his death and his key fragment surrendered, the rival clans are broken. The Gelkis are poised to conquer the wastes."}},[79]={k="1480",["end"]={d=1488,t="A vile contract written on flayed skin set you on the hunt for Lord Azrethoc. To track the hidden evil, you tore a scalp from a Hatefury satyr and stole a flawless crystal from the coastal naga. When the scrying ritual revealed a monster of terrible power, the burden of his execution fell to you. You marched south, striking down the demon lord and his warlock servant in the dust. Azrethoc's grip on the Burning Blade is forever broken. Through your ruthless victory, the Warchief's enemies are crippled, and the Horde's future in this desolate land grows just a little brighter."}},[82]={k="6141",["end"]={d=1053,t="You crossed the sea to Desolace, seeking a righteous war alongside Brother Anton. To prove your devotion, you shattered the rotting dead in the Valley of Bones, earning a seal of commendation for the Scarlet Crusade. But when you carried that seal back east to Southshore, you learned a bitter truth from Raleigh the Devout. The Crusade's holy war had twisted into a paranoid slaughter, torturing innocents in the name of the Light. Instead of joining their ranks, you breached their monastery and broke their deranged regime. Your blade ended a creeping madness, sparing countless lives from the pyre."}},[107]={k="1238",["end"]={d=7541,t="You dug an agent's severed head from the swamp muck and sought the dark magic of the Darkspear to give his spirit voice. Through a bubbling cauldron, Marg Nighteye confessed his final failure. You hunted the beast that claimed his life and recovered his prize: a noble's pendant of human craftsmanship, held by mere soldiers near Theramore. Now, that glittering jewel rests in Orgrimmar with Zor Lonetree. Though the scholars have only just begun to study its origins, you have honored a fallen spy's last wish and placed a piece of a dangerous Alliance mystery into the hands of the Horde."}},[108]={k="1251",["end"]={d=1276,t="You pried a blackened iron shield from the charred chimney of the ruined Shady Rest Inn. Hoping it held a clue to the attackers, you brought the heavy metal to Krog, who passed it to the blacksmith Do'gol. After you gathered venom from the marsh's giant spiders to strip away the soot, a name emerged: Mosarn. The trail led you high into Thunder Bluff to question the craftsman himself. He recognized his own work, but the revelation brought only frustration. Mosarn had forged too many pieces to remember a single buyer. The scorched shield remains a dead end, leaving the ashes of the inn unavenged."}},[110]={k="1321",["end"]={d=1276,t="You brought a heavy, scorched shield to Krog, hoping its blackened metal held answers. When Do'gol the blacksmith needed a solvent to clear away the soot, you harvested acidic venom from the massive Darkfang spiders of the marsh. The corrosive bile revealed a single name etched into the rim: Mosarn. Carrying this solitary clue all the way to Thunder Bluff, you finally found the master craftsman. Yet, for all your efforts, the truth remains obscured. Mosarn easily recognized his own handiwork, but his memory of its owner was as blank as the darkened steel. The trail has gone completely cold."}},[111]={k="1260",["end"]={d=1271,t="You traveled far from the safety of Stormwind's taverns to help craft a menu for the Blue Recluse. In the sweltering mire of Dustwallow Marsh, you hunted mudrock turtles for their rare tongues. From there, you journeyed to the distant Swamp of Sorrows, wading through the muck to harvest flawless crab legs from the beasts lurking in its waters. It was grueling work in the most unforgiving bogs of the world. Yet your grim labor bore rich fruit. Angus Stern welcomed you back from the mud with a grand feast in your honor, cementing your place as a celebrated guest at the finest table in the city."}},[113]={k="1252",["end"]={d=1287,t="You pulled a charred badge from the rubble, bearing the name of Lieutenant Paval Reethe. Bringing it to the guards of Theramore uncovered a bitter truth. Reethe was no fallen hero, but a deserter still loyal to the late Admiral Daelin. You tracked his former comrades to the ruins of Lost Point, only to learn that even they had cast Reethe out for recklessly provoking the nearby ogres. Now, Theramore prepares to march on the deserters' camp and hunt the rogue lieutenant down. What began as a simple discovery in the ashes has sparked a purge of the dissidents festering in the marsh."}},[114]={k="1259",["end"]={d=1287,t="You went digging into the name of Lieutenant Paval Reethe. The records of Adjutant Tesoran revealed a distinguished Kul Tiras marine marked only as missing. But Captain Vimes knew the bitter truth: Reethe was a traitor, a fanatical loyalist to Admiral Daelin. Hunting for answers, you tracked a band of these deserters to an abandoned watchtower at Lost Point and broke their leader, Balos Jacken. The rogue confessed they had abandoned Reethe for recklessly plotting to raid the ogres of Brackenwall Village. You delivered this vital intelligence back to Theramore. The guard now marches to crush the deserter camp, and the rogue lieutenant's days in the merciless marsh are numbered."}},[116]={k="1169",["end"]={d=1173,t="You gathered the remains of the beasts that drove the Stonemaul Clan from their home, allowing Draz'Zilb to trace the threat to Onyxia's brood. When Overlord Mok'Morokk cowered in the face of the black dragonflight, you took matters into your own hands. You waded into the Wyrmbog, smashing the dragonlord's eggs to halt the spreading menace. With the breeding grounds shattered, you turned your blade toward the unworthy overlord himself. You battered the cowardly Mok'Morokk until he fled into the marsh. Through your strength, the ogres are finally free to choose a worthy leader and march south to reclaim their stolen village."}},[117]={k="783",["end"]={d=54,t="You answered the call when the armies of Stormwind were stretched thin. By the order of Marshal McBride, you proved your worth by culling the kobold infestation at the Echo Ridge Mine, driving back the thieves before they could deepen their foothold in Northshire. For your relentless efforts, you carried sealed documents south to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire, earning the title of Acting Deputy. It is a grim promotion. With the true army entangled in the distant whims of nobles, the safety of Elwynn Forest now rests heavily upon your shoulders."}},[125]={k="2862",["end"]={d=7732,t="You started by culling the desperate Woodpaw gnolls outside Camp Mojache, only to discover they were fleeing a greater nightmare. Their crude battle plans pointed south to the Writhing Deep, where an unknown enemy swarmed. You ventured into the insect hive, slaughtering the massive Stinglasher and harvesting its glands for study. Carrying this grim intelligence to Orgrimmar, you brought the truth to Zilzibin Drumlore. The beasts driving the gnolls are silithid, an ancient horror the Horde has foolishly ignored. You secured the outpost, but unmasked a subterranean menace that dwarfs any petty faction war."}},[126]={k="2866",["end"]={d=2871,t="You went to the Ruins of Solarsal to uncover why the Hatecrest naga had swarmed the ancient stones. Finding a warm, glyph-carved gazebo, you returned to Feathermoon Stronghold to mount an offensive. You slaughtered the serpentine invaders for their scales, then pushed across the water to the Isle of Dread to assassinate Lord Shalzaru. With the cruel royal dead, the Hatecrest threat is broken, buying the stronghold precious time. But the strange, alien relic you tore from his hands now sits with Vestia Moonspear, leaving an unsettling mystery quietly resting within her care."}},[130]={k="4124",["end"]={d=4267,t="You set out to find a missing courier, tracking Raschal from a shattered rowboat to the camps of the Woodpaw gnolls. Guided by strange magic and abandoned baggage, your hunt led into the Writhing Deep, where you tore the man from an alien Zukk'ash pod. But saving one life unearthed a far greater nightmare. General Shandris Feathermoon sent you to Darnassus with a grim report of the infestation. There, Gracina Spiritmight revealed the true nature of those insects. They are the silithid. What began as a simple rescue in Feralas has exposed a devastating menace, a looming shadow threatening to consume everything."},mid={d=4130,t="You sought out Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold to aid his search for a lost courier. Journeying down the coast of Feralas, you found Raschal’s rowboat shredded to splinters in the shallows. In the muddy waters below, you unearthed his sunken knife. Seeking answers, Ginro sent you to Quintis Jonespyre, a druid capable of drawing history from the blade. Through the magic of psychometry, Quintis witnessed Raschal's final known moments. The courier clashed with Woodpaw gnolls, but it was not the beasts that filled him with terror, nor the water elementals rising from the depths behind his back. You delivered this grim vision to Ginro, confirming that Raschal faced a far darker threat. Yet the true source of his fear, and his ultimate fate in the wilds, remain an absolute mystery."}},[133]={k="3121",mid={d=3124,t="You carried a macabre token, a dwarven shrunken head, into the dark depths of Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. In exchange, Neeru Fireblade handed over a potent herbal mixture, the catalyst for Witch Doctor Uzer'i's strange magic. With those herbs, Uzer'i enchanted a vessel designed to trap a dying creature's very essence. You took this dark artifact to the Hinterlands, testing it first on Elune's savage owlbeasts. As they fell, you bound their spirits, trapping their muisek before it could seek vengeance. You did the same to the noble frayfeather hippogryphs. Now Uzer'i holds the trapped essence of these fierce, wild creatures in his hands. You have mastered the dangerous art of capturing their souls, but to what dark end the witch doctor plans to use this gathered power remains a mystery."},["end"]={d=3129,t="You carried a grisly trade to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar, exchanging a shrunken head for the herbs needed to trap souls. Armed with Uzer'i's prepared muisek vessel, you stalked the ancient forests of the Hinterlands to slaughter the sacred allies of the night elves. You bound the vengeful spirits of fierce owlbeasts alongside loyal hippogryphs. You trapped elusive faerie dragons and felled ancient wandering treants. Finally, you brought down the towering mountain giants before their essence could flee. Now, Uzer'i has forged these captive spirits into mortal steel. The primal strength of these fallen protectors is forever chained to your hands, empowering the Horde."}},[134]={k="3125",["end"]={d=3129,t="You hunted down the ancient allies of the night elves, turning their very spirits into tools for the Horde. First, you stripped the magical essence from the delicate sprite darters. Next, you tore the protective souls from the lumbering wandering forest walkers. Finally, you felled the towering mountain giants, trapping their massive power within Witch Doctor Uzer'i's vessels. His dark ritual is now complete. The stolen strength of the wilderness was permanently bound into steel and wood. You walked away wielding the might of the forest itself, a heavy weapon forged from captured souls."}},[137]={k="2939",["end"]={d=2942,t="You carried a mysterious stave from the overgrown ruins of Feralas to Darnassus, seeking answers. To pry a history book from Daryn Lightwind, you traveled the world, wielding Curgle Cranklehop's crude camera to capture a massive turtle in the Hinterlands. Returning to Troyas Moonbreeze, the hard-earned knowledge revealed the stave's true purpose. Armed with ancient fire, you plunged into the Ruins of Ravenwind, awakening the Equinex Monolith from its slumber. From its cold heart, you pulled the Morrow Stone. Though its full power remains a mystery, you have unearthed a relic of immense significance, rescuing a piece of ancient history from the wilds."}},[138]={k="2969",["end"]={d=4298,t="You stood against the fierce Grimtotem clan in Feralas, fighting alongside the Moonweavers to tear open cages and set the captive faerie dragons loose. Your deeds reached the ear of High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind herself. But the true weight of your journey rested in a single, fragile egg. You carried that unborn sprite darter across the world, seeking the wisdom of Quentin and the beast handler Agnar in the distant Hinterlands to keep it safe. You gathered the fresh meat it needed to survive, and through your fierce protection, the shell finally broke. A tiny, winged life emerged, safe at last in the hands of its new guardian."},mid={d=3841,t="Deep in the wilds of Feralas, you broke the Grimtotem clan's cruel cages, freeing the captive faerie dragons alongside the Moonweaver sisters. Not content with mere rescue, you turned your blades upon the tauren camp, dealing brutal retribution for their poaching. Your valor carried you all the way to the boughs of Teldrassil, where you presented Jer'kai's signet ring to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind. Though the High Priestess dispatched scouts to watch over the sisters, your own part in this tale was not yet finished. You brought a rare, nearly mature sprite darter egg to Quentin, saving the orphan from the same poachers you slaughtered. The egg rests before you, fragile and full of life, but whether this tiny creature will safely hatch and survive to spread its wings remains a mystery."}},[159]={k="659",["end"]={d=661,t="The savage mutation of a dog named Stanley in Hillsbrad drew you into a web of Forsaken intrigue. At Phin Odelic's behest, you sought his missing companions in the Arathi Highlands. Finding Quae and Kinelory watching Go'Shek Farm, you intercepted a courier and uncovered Apothecary Jorell's dark experiments. You fought alongside Kinelory to raid the farm and steal the remaining research, bringing the grim evidence safely back to Southshore. Though the full scope of the undead's sinister work remains shadowed, Phin now has the proof he needs. Because of your blade, the plague spreaders suffered a heavy blow, and three friends live to fight another day."}},[162]={k="1450",["end"]={d=1469,t="You sought answers about Brohann Caskbelly's lost expedition. Falstad Wildhammer pointed you to Gryphon Master Talonaxe, who recalled a brilliant rider ruined by drink: Rhapsody Shindigger. You tracked the disgraced dwarf to his remote camp, finding him lost in a haze of ale. To loosen his tongue, you crossed the sea to Kalimdor, hunting beasts across Tanaris and Feralas to brew him a fierce concoction. The liquor finally stirred his memory of a drunken fall into a swamp, revealing a sunken temple swarming with trolls. You delivered his stolen Atal'ai artifact to Brohann, proving the ancient ruins were real, and hiding beneath the dark waters."}},[188]={k="1109",["end"]={d=1113,t="You descended into the muck of Razorfen Kraul, scraping foul guano from the roosts of the rare Kraul Bats. But the Royal Apothecary Society required more than mere filth for their grand experiment. You marched to the peaks of Tirisfal Glades, butchering the fanatical members of the Scarlet Crusade within the Scarlet Monastery to tear the beating hearts from their chests. Now, you have delivered these bloody prizes to the Master. In these shadowed halls, clashing elements will be fused with deadly toxins. You have provided the catalyst for a new, ghastly creation born of blind zealotry and festering decay."}},[199]={k="3441",["end"]={d=3481,t="You became Kalaran Windblade's instrument of vengeance against the Dark Iron dwarves. To cripple their defenses, you harvested elemental flames, shattered thorium blades, and stole a heathen idol to forge the Torch of Retribution. When you grasped the weapon, its raw hatred pulsed into your very veins. Guided by Squire Maltrake, you carried that spite into the enemy's sentry towers, engulfing them in an inextinguishable blaze. The dwarven lines are broken, their fortifications reduced to a blinding inferno. Yet as you finally claim your prize from a black dragon's hoard, you are left to wonder who truly orchestrated this glorious devastation."},mid={d=3452,t="Kalaran Windblade shared a grim tale, drawing you into his scheme for vengeance. To strike a crippling blow against his foes, he planned to reduce four sentry towers to ash. Ordinary fire would not suffice, so you hunted elementals and golems across the wastes, harvesting fiery hearts and oil for a flawless flame. You then stripped enchanted thorium daggers from brutal Dark Iron slavers to forge a sturdy shaft. Finally, you ascended the mountains to slay the Twilight's Hammer cultists, claiming a dark symbol of Ragnaros to serve as a magical casing. With the foul magic secured, the torch is now whole. You hold the means to ignite the towers, but the true consequences of Kalaran's retribution remain shrouded in mystery."}},[223]={k="1274",["end"]={d=1247,t="Young Thomas steered you to Bishop DeLavey, pulling you into a quiet conspiracy. A diplomat bound for Theramore vanished without a trace. Moving in the shadows, you carried sealed letters from Jorgen to the cheesemaker Elling Trias. This trail of whispers led to Watcher Backus in Duskwood, where you unearthed Defias documents at Addle's Stead. The papers outlined a sinister plot, but the final piece required beating the truth out of Dashel Stonefist in an alley. His bloody confession revealed a backup plan run by an inside man named Slim. Your brutal footwork cracked the plot wide open, shifting the desperate search to Menethil."},mid={d=1243,t="A quiet word from young Thomas drew you into the shadowed halls of Stormwind Keep. There, Bishop DeLavey entrusted you with a heavy secret: a diplomat bound for Theramore had vanished without a trace. Suspecting the Defias, the bishop directed you to his hidden contacts. You found the grudging Jorgen in the Valley of Heroes, who passed a sealed note for you to carry to Elling Trias in the Trade District. The cheesemaker quickly dropped his guise of a simple merchant, tapping into his covert network to point you down a much darker road. Now you stand under the gloomy canopy of Duskwood, questioning Watcher Backus about recent Defias movements. But the fate of the missing diplomat, and the true depths of the conspiracy that stole them away, still remain hidden in the shadows."}},[225]={k="583",["end"]={d=208,t="You arrived in the sweltering wilds of Stranglethorn as a stranger, seeking the wisdom of Hemet Nesingwary. To prove your worth, you waded into the thick foliage, thinning the local raptor packs before claiming the talon of the cunning Tethis. Having matched wits against the jungle's finest predators, you finally set your sights on the expedition's ultimate prize. Deep in the wilderness, you cornered and slew the legendary white tiger, King Bangalash. Returning with this final trophy, you earned the absolute respect of a renowned war hero. Your mastery of the hunt is now unquestioned."}},[227]={k="215",["end"]={d=331,t="You rescued Private Thorsen and learned of his secret mission to infiltrate Kurzen's forces. Realizing a traitor had exposed him, you raided Bookie Herod's records and uncovered a hidden key. Deep within the enemy stockpile, you opened a secure strongbox to find a muddy note tracking Thorsen's every move. By cross-referencing the camp's patrol schedules with the letter's signature, you unmasked Private Merle as the informant. Though the betrayal cuts deep, your discovery has purged a deadly rot from the rebel ranks. Without a spy feeding their secrets to a corrupt colonel, these desperate outcasts finally stand a chance."}},[231]={k="2842",["end"]={d=2843,t="Word of Kernobee's discovery sent you seeking a swift path to Gnomeregan. You crossed the sea from Ratchet to the tropical shores of Booty Bay to find Scooty and his volatile Transpolyporter 6000. Despite the goblin's reassurances about its explosive history, you allowed him to calibrate a personal transponder to your exact size and weight. The perilous overland trek through the frozen, dwarf-infested peaks of Dun Morogh is now a thing of the past. With a single, brave step onto the pad, the irradiated depths of Gnomeregan await you in a blinding flash, bridging continents in a heartbeat."}},[236]={k="616",["end"]={d=611,t="A tavern rumor in Booty Bay sent you hunting for a fabled troll relic. You braved a haunted island off Stranglethorn and discovered the cursed goblin mage Gazban. To break his affliction, you carried elemental remnants to Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver in Dalaran. His wisdom directed you back to his pirate daughter Catelyn, who needed you to reclaim an ancient dagger from a Bloodsail Buccaneer. Plunging that blade into a sunken altar beneath the waves shattered the enchantment. You delivered the Stone of the Tides to Baron Revilgaz. The magnificent Gurubashi artifact now rests securely in his private collection, a testament to your relentless efforts."}},[240]={k="606",["end"]={d=613,t="You became the heavy hand of a ruthless gambler. To settle Sea Wolf MacKinley's ledgers, you played on a coward's fears, using gorilla gore to extort coin from Shaky Phillipe. When simple threats were not enough, you stalked the cursed ruins of Aboraz and Jubuwal to claim the dues of the undead. You severed the locked club foot right off Maury Wilkins, then slaughtered your way through the Mosh'Ogg ogre mound just to find its key. Now, the dead man's hollow leg is finally cracked open, and MacKinley has his bloody prize. The debts are settled, leaving your pockets heavy and your hands forever stained."}},[247]={k="9609",["end"]={d=1425,t="You found Watcher Biggs stranded in the murky swamp, the sole survivor of a brutal ambush by the Lost Ones. After holding back the wild beasts drawn to his ruined camp, you pushed into the Fallow Sanctuary to reclaim the stolen reagents the Nethergarde wizards desperately needed. With sun-dried driftwood gathered from the eastern coast to repair his broken wagon, you carried the caravan's most vital supplies south into the desolate Blasted Lands. By delivering those salvaged crystals to Quartermaster Lungertz, you ensured Nethergarde Keep can continue its lonely, crucial watch over the Dark Portal. Because of you, the Alliance's defenses hold strong."}},[248]={k="698",["end"]={d=1428,t="You journeyed to the desolate eastern coast, hauling fresh sawtooth meat to feed an isolated Horde outpost. To arm the camp, you harvested razor-sharp claws from the beasts, supplying Tok'Kar with the means to craft rugged weapons. But true security demanded a bloodier toll. Directed by Katar's bitter hatred for the ocean's spawn, you carved a relentless path through the murloc tribes polluting the shore. Their gurgling cries were silenced, their ranks broken upon the sand. You leave the beach soaked in the blood of the fish men, bearing a newly forged weapon as a grim token of your slaughter. The encroaching sea has been pushed back."}},[255]={k="992A",["end"]={d=162,t="You set out to map dry wells for Gadgetzan, only to unearth a creeping horror in the sands. From the drained pools of the Noxious Lair to the remains of a lost goblin deep within the Gaping Chasm, you faced a swarm driven by a sinister, unseen will. Alchemist Pestlezugg’s findings confirmed the worst—these were no mindless beasts. You carried that grim warning all the way to Darnassus. There, Gracina Spiritmight gave your enemy a name: the silithid. What started as a dispute over desert water has laid bare an ancient, ravenous menace threatening all of Kalimdor."}},[256]={k="992H",["end"]={d=32,t="You went looking for water near Sandsorrow Watch, but found a desert drained by ravenous insects. From the Centipaar in the Noxious Lair to the lost surveyor Scrimshank in the Gaping Chasm, you tracked this creeping horror. Alchemist Pestlezugg confirmed your worst fears: an unseen, malignant will drove these mindless ravagers. You carried this grim truth across the sands to Orgrimmar, where Zilzibin Drumlore finally gave the nightmare a name. The silithid have risen. What started as a simple drought is now an apocalyptic threat to all of Azeroth."}},[259]={k="8576",["end"]={d=8606,t="Azuregos’s ledger held the secrets of an ancient device, but its Draconic text baffled Narain Soothfancy. To decipher it, you sought the gnome's buried translation manual south of Land's End Beach, only to find an empty hole and a crudely pasted ransom note. Enraged by the extortion, Narain dressed you in his robes and a turban, sending you into the freezing snows of Winterspring with a bag of rocks to spring a trap. But the cunning thieves slipped through your fingers. The ambush failed, the manual vanished, and you realized you had gravely underestimated these unseen foes."}},[261]={k="8922",["end"]={d=8928,t="Deliana’s desperate need to commune with the ghost of Anthion Harmon sent you to the eccentric Mux Manascrambler. To fuel his mad genius, you scoured the world's most perilous edges. You forged a distiller from volcanic ash, harvested the lingering anguish of tortured spirits across three continents, and tore a beating magma core from an elemental lord. Finally, braving a demon-infested gorge to secure a channeling rod, your tireless efforts have borne fruit. Mux has assembled his intricate machine. The veil between worlds is finally pierced, and at last, the dead are ready to speak."}},[262]={k="8923",["end"]={d=8928,t="You traveled to the ends of the world for Mux Manascrambler, piecing together a machine to pierce the veil of death. You gathered volcanic ash from the Burning Steppes and harvested the haunted ectoplasm of tormented spirits across Silithus, Winterspring, and the Plaguelands. To power the bizarre contraption, you tore a molten core from Magma Lord Bokk himself, then braved the depths of Darkwhisper Gorge to purchase a specialized channeling rod. Now, the device is finally complete. With these rare components united, the barrier between worlds has weakened, and Mokvar's desperate hope to speak with the fallen Anthion is at last within reach."}},[276]={k="1104",["end"]={d=1194,t="You helped Fizzle Brassbolts push the limits of his racing machines, securing scorpid venom for fuel and tracking down Martek the Exiled in the harsh Badlands. Martek discovered that indurium flakes could withstand immense heat, pointing the gnomes toward Uldaman for pure ore. Yet loyalty on the salt flats is fleeting. Aided by Zamek's distraction, you slipped into the gnomes' camp and stole Rizzle Brassbolts' schematics. Handing the stolen indurium sample over to Pozzik, you leveled the playing field. Now both factions know the metallic prize hidden deep within the earth, ensuring their fierce rivalry will burn hotter than ever."}},[278]={k="1176",["end"]={d=1189,t="You scoured the salt flats for vulture bones to lighten Pozzik's racers. When a promised fuel regulator went missing, you chased its trail from Gazlowe in Ratchet to the wharves of Booty Bay. You stole the blueprints right from under Cozzle's nose, handing the goblin team the edge they craved. But engineering was not enough for their reckless pilot, Razzeric. You salvaged a volatile seaforium booster from a crashed zeppelin and brought it to Shreev in Gadgetzan to strip away its safety limits. You have handed a madman a bomb strapped to an engine. The great rivalry is forever changed."},mid={d=1182,t="You arrived at the salt flats looking for speed, harvesting bones to shave weight from Pozzik’s machines. But lightweight frames couldn't guarantee victory against the gnomes. The goblin needed a prototype fuel regulator, sparking a chase across the sea. Gazlowe in Ratchet had no answers, and Wharfmaster Lozgil found empty ledgers in Booty Bay. The trail ended with Baron Revilgaz, who admitted the part was never built. You marched into the Stranglethorn jungles, cracking the locks of Cozzle's home to steal the Venture Company foreman's blueprints yourself. Revilgaz claimed the schematics to make his copies, preparing to send you back to the racers. The hard work is done, but the outcome remains unknown. Will these stolen designs finally give Pozzik the edge he so desperately craves, or is his team already doomed to eat gnome dust?"}},[303]={k="79008",["end"]={d=79980,t="A blistered note plucked from a dying fire first set you on this grim trail. It led to a charred corpse and a dark revelation: botched deliveries of the New Plague disguised as apothecary accidents. Following the dead man's directions, you climbed into the rugged peaks between the Barrens and Desolace. A treacherous descent from his hidden camp finally ended in the dirt. There, you unearthed a buried messenger bag stocked with survival supplies and a soiled parchment. You followed the breadcrumbs to a secret stash, proving you have stumbled into a deadly conspiracy far larger than a few scattered ashes."}},[304]={k="463",["end"]={d=98283,t="You sought Rethiel the Greenwarden deep within the bogs of the Wetlands, answering his call to heal a suffering ecosystem. To restore balance, you culled the encroaching Mosshide gnolls near the gates of Algaz and stripped away their flints to protect the living wood. When the marsh blistered with diseased fen creepers, you laid the shambling horrors to rest. Finally, beneath Raptor Ridge, you used malignant flesh to draw out a maddened alpha raptor known as Carnage. Slaying the beast brought a desperate peace to the Razormaw pack. Through your bloody work, the wounded wetlands finally have time to mend."}}},
